\par\par \b \uc2 SNAPSHOT-India stocks, bonds, rupee, swaps, call closing levels\b0\par\par\uc2 333 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2012\par 14:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2    STOCKS         \tab \par -----------------------    \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's main 30-share BSE index closed 1.72 percent higher at 16,222.30 points, while the broader 50-share NSE index\f28 \par \par \uc2 ended 1.77 percent higher at 4,921.40 points.\par \par \uc2 A steep hike in petrol prices boosted oil stocks such as ONGC\par \par \uc2 by kindling hopes of similar hikes in other fuels such as diesel, though doubts emerged about government action after \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the markets closed.  \tab \par      \tab \par GOVERNMENT BONDS      \tab \par -------------------------------      \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's benchmark bond yield ended 1 basis point lower at 8.50 percent, hitting earlier its lowest in over a month, after a sharp hike in petrol prices led to hopes for more fiscal discipline from the government.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par RUPEE      \tab \par --------------      \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rupee ended 55.65/66 per dollar, recovering from the day's low of 56.40, boosted by hopes the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would sell dollars directly to oil companies, taking out a major chunk of dollar demand from the spot market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rupee also gained as traders saw sporadic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , while other traders cited dollar selling by custodian banks as well as exporters converting their foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  holdings on the last day of the two-week deadline mandated recently by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It had closed at 55.9950/56.0050 on Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INTEREST RATE SWAPS      \tab \par ----------------------------      \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The one-year OIS and the five-year rate\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 were up 1 bps at 8.01 percent and 7.48 percent respectively.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CALL MONEY      \tab \par --------------------      \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's overnight cash rate ended at 8.15/8.20 percent, lower than Wednesday's close of 8.25/8.30 percent. Market participants are watching out for more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to gauge the impact on liquidity.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ----------------------      \tab \par  Double click on codes in      \tab \par  Reuters MIOR/MIBOR                                    \tab \par  NSE MIBID/MIBOR                                     \tab \par  Reuters Corporate Bond Yield/Spread            \tab \par  For Reuters Benchmarks                            \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Asia markets technicals - (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.reuterstechnicals.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.reuterstechnicals.com}}}\uc2 \f2 )\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Compiled by Archana Narayanan)\f28 \par \par \uc2 INDIA-SNAPSHOT/ | ABN | D | M | RBN | SNI | SNS | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120524e85o000tb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
