\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indian rupee rebounds from record low; snaps losing run\b0\par\par\uc2 516 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2012\par 14:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupee recovers after hitting new record low at 56.40\par \par \uc2 * RBI does not rule out selling USD to oil companies\par \par \uc2 * Exporters also seen selling foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings\par \par \uc2 (Updates with paragraph on petrol price impact)\par \par \uc2 By Swati Bhat\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 24 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee posted its first gain against the dollar in four sessions on Thursday, recovering from a new record low earlier in the session, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor did not rule out selling dollars directly to oil importers.\par \par \uc2 Making dollars available for oil companies would remove a sizeable source of demand for the greenback from the market, and help support the rupee, which has hit record lows over the last seven consecutive sessions.\par \par \uc2 The rupee also gained as traders saw sporadic \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while other traders cited dollar selling by custodian banks as well as exporters converting their foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings on the last day of the two-week deadline mandated recently by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 No wide impact was seen from the government's decision on Wednesday to allow a hike in petrol prices, especially as doubts emerged about whether policy makers would follow up with hikes in other fuels such as diesel that would have a bigger impact on fiscal consolidation.\par \par \uc2 "The statement from RBI was a positive for the market but I believe there were also genuine flows in the market after a long time. Foreign banks were major sellers today," said Paresh Nayar, head of fixed income and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  at First Rand Bank.\par \par \uc2 The rupee closed at 55.65/66 per dollar after hitting a record low of 56.40 hit earlier in the session. The pair had closed Wednesday at 55.9950/56.0050 on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The rupee has shed 12.7 percent against the dollar since its 2012 peak in early February and is the worst performer in Asia so far this year.\par \par \uc2 After \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively earlier this month, traders say the RBI has appeared to hold back in recent days, reluctant to fight the intense global risk aversion that is pushing up the dollar.\par \par \uc2 However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen selling dollars on Wednesday, and some saw signs of action on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "There was a lot of selling from state-run banks as well today, which could probably have been on behalf of the RBI but custodian flows were also very good," a senior trader at a Japanese Bank said.\par \par \uc2 Thursday was the last day in which exporters had to convert their foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their accounts.\par \par \uc2 The one-month offshore non-deliverable forward rates were quoted at 56.05 while the three-month NDF was at 56.82.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most-traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and the United Stock Exchange all ended around 55.72 on a total volume of $6.7 billion.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Rafael Nam)\par \par \uc2 INDIA-RUPEE/ (CLOSER) (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | SNI | SNS | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120527e85o0004j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
