\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee breaks below 55/dlr to record low\b0\par\par\uc2 422 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2012\par 14:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupee drops to latest record low; outlook weak\par \par \uc2 * RBI not spotted but traders expect measures\par \par \uc2 * Near-term NDFs signal more falls in the rupee\par \par \uc2 By Swati Bhat\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 21 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee fell below the key psychological level of 55 to hit a new record low on Monday, setting up the prospect of further falls unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  takes measures or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  more aggressively, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The rupee has now hit four consecutive record lows in as many sessions, at a time of intense turmoil over the euro zone, but traders saw no major signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  either on Friday or on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Despite the absence, traders are bracing for new measures from the RBI. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has largely failed to prevent the rupee's falls this month despite selling dollars and taking steps to attract inflows via deposits and exporters' foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings.\par \par \uc2 Traders say the Indian rupee, which is Asia's worst-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, has proven particularly vulnerable to the global risk aversion given the steep fiscal and economic challenges facing the country.\par \par \uc2 "With just six months worth import cover, twin deficits, lack of confidence in the coalition government with regards to reforms, and also failure to attract foreign flows, suggests the INR is likely to hit 56-56.50 in the next two months," said Pramod Patil, a \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at \uc2 United Overseas Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible unit hit a life-time low of 55.05 per dollar during the session, before closing at 55.03/04, according to SBI data, well below its 54.42/44 close on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Also weighing on the rupee was dollar demand from oil firms and corporates, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Although profit-taking in the USD/INR cross could temper the pace of falls in the local unit in the near-term, the outlook for the rupee still remains very weak unless global risk aversion eases, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The one-month NDF was quoted at 55.45 while the three month NDF was at 56.10, both indicative of the expectations for further falls.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most-traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and the United Stock Exchange all ended around 55.09 on a total volume of $4.35 billion.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Rafael Nam)\par \par \uc2 INDIA-RUPEE/ (CLOSER) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | SNI | SNS | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120524e85l000pj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
