\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET EYE FOCUS-In rupee fall, RBI may target oil next\b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2012\par 11:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  As the rupee plumbs to record lows against the dollar, traders say the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  could go beyond \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and target dollar demand from oil companies, an approach that if done right may just help stem the rout.\par \par \uc2  Having proved unable to contain the rupee's falls via its actions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, the RBI was widely reported to have met oil companies this week, and a look at the numbers shows why.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers estimate average daily demand for dollars from state-run oil refiners at around $400-$500 million, with demand peaking towards the end of the month when they are supposed to make payments.\par \par \uc2  Targeting oil could succeed, but it will come down to how the RBI does it, traders say.\par \par \uc2  The RBI is widely seen to have two options: it could open a dollar window for oil companies to buy dollars directly from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or it could purchase oil bonds via special market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  RBI opted for the latter in 2008 and then again in 2009 because oil companies back then were holding illiquid bonds. That helped the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  both inject dollar liquidity and help the sector monetise its debt. \par \par \uc2  However, 2012 would be different. Oil companies no longer hold much outstanding oil bonds a nd traders see a far more effective approach if the RBI were to sell dollars directly to the sector.\par \par \uc2  "The direct dollar window to oil firms can help the rupee recover to around 53.80 per dollar. Oil prices also have come down by 10-15 percent, that will also help the rupee over the next 30-60 days horizon," a dealer in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  and rates at a private bank said. \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Subhadip Sircar, Swati Bhat & Suvashree Dey Choudhury)\par \par \uc2 MARKETEYE-FOCUS/SMO | ABN | D | M | SNI | SNS   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120521e85i000i0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
