\par\par \b \uc2 2nd UPDATE: India  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Official:  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Reserves Adequate For  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Actions\b0\par\par\uc2 517 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2012\par 14:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Data show India's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at over 19-month low\par \par \uc2 -- Will take all steps needed to stabilize rupee, deputy governor says\par \par \uc2 -- Wide current-account deficit responsible for rupee's losses\par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves data in 3rd paragraph, updates \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  level in 5th paragraph.)\par \par \uc2 By Abhrajit Gangopadhyay and Sudeep Jain\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 KOLKATA (Dow Jones)--India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are adequate for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue to take actions to stabilize the rupee, a top official said Friday, even as data showed the reserves fell to a more than 19-month low last week.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  will use all its available tools to fulfill its stated objective of curbing volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Deputy Governor Subir Gokarn said on the sidelines of a conference in the eastern Indian city of Kolkata.\par \par \uc2 His comments come amid concerns that the RBI's ability to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is limited by \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's modest \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. According to data released by the RBI Friday, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell by $1.37 billion to $291.8 billion in the week ended May 11.\par \par \uc2 The RBI has been seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the market in recent weeks to arrest the rupee's relentless slide against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The local unit sank to a record low for the third straight day Friday as investors dumped risk-sensitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  following poor U.S. manufacturing data and heightened fears that Greece will leave the euro zone. The greenback was quoted at INR54.42 late Friday in Asia, after trading as high as INR54.90 earlier in the session.\par \par \uc2 "Our approach over the last few months has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when we felt the rupee would stabilize, and some administrative actions," Gokarn said.\par \par \uc2 Unlike many other emerging economies which have trade surpluses and large \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, India runs wide trade and current-account deficits. The country's current \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are adequate to finance merchandise imports for less than six-and-a-half months and reserves need to be built up, according to CLSA.\par \par \uc2 Besides selling dollars, the RBI has also in recent weeks forced exporters to convert half of their foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings into rupees, and raised the interest-rate ceiling on local foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits of Indians living abroad.\par \par \uc2 Gokarn said the rupee's slump is mostly due to India's structural problem of a wide current-account deficit.\par \par \uc2 Also, in the past few sessions, the dollar has strengthened across the globe, contributing to the pressure on the rupee, he added.\par \par \uc2 India's current-account deficit, which is widely expected to have exceeded 4% of gross domestic product in the fiscal year ended March 31, is seen as the biggest weight on the rupee.\par \par \uc2 The country's dependence on volatile portfolio capital flows to fill its current-account deficit makes the rupee especially vulnerable to bouts of risk aversion.\par \par \uc2 -By Abhrajit Gangopadhyay and Sudeep Jain, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 6145 6123; sudeep.jain@dowjones.com [ 18-05-12 1239GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120518e85i000si\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
