\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Emerging stocks plunge 2.5 pct, central banks act\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sujata Rao   \par \uc2 613 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2012\par 10:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds quotes)\par \par \uc2 LONDON, May 16 (Reuters) - Emerging equities plunged 2.7 percent on Wednesday and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell heavily, forcing several central banks to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as investors fearing a noisy Greek exit from the euro fled for the safety of U.S. dollar assets.\par \par \uc2 Investor flight from higher-risk assets has accelerated after Greek politicians' failure to form a coalition government paved the way for fresh elections and focused attention on the consequences of an exit from the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 Markets were battered across emerging Asia and Europe, with MSCI's main emerging equity index headed for its biggest one-day loss in six months and on the brink of erasing all its gains for 2012.\par \par \uc2 "As long as we have this Greek uncertainty hanging over the market, investors will remain in risk-off mode ... you sell emerging markets and you buy the dollar, U.S. and German bonds," said Murat Toprak, emerging markets strategist at \uc2 HSBC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The big question is what will the Fed and ECB policymakers do?" Toprak said, referring to the growing expectation that the U.S. Federal Reserve and European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will soon announce plans for more quantitative easing.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the session, Chinese stocks, which make up a fifth of the emerging index, fell 1.2 percent to a one-month low\par \par \uc2 while Indian and Korean markets slid 2 percent and 3 percent respectively.\par \par \uc2 In emerging Europe, Russian stocks led the rout, falling 2.5 percent and now almost 5 percent down on the year. The mining and oil-heavy index has suffered from the recent weakness in commodity prices, with Brent crude futures having slid almost $10 a barrel since the start of May.\par \par \uc2 The massive equity falls took a toll on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , forcing many central banks into action. The Polish zloty rose off four-month lows versus the euro after state bank BGK was sighted selling euros on the spot market.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, India's rupee, exposed by the country's current account gap, fell to record lows to the dollar sparking \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  while Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also reported to have acted to help the won which posted its biggest one-day loss this year.\par \par \uc2 "If \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  overshoot, central banks will be back to protect them, especially in countries where inflation is an issue as in Poland or Turkey," Toprak predicted.\par \par \uc2 He said he was not at the moment recommending clients to hold long positions in any emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in emerging Europe there were heavy losses on the Russian rouble which shed almost 1 percent against the dollar\par \par \uc2 while the Hungarian forint, vulnerable to risk appetite swings, also fell more than 1 percent against the euro at one point.\par \par \uc2 "Eastern European countries have economic ties to the region and therefore we see some of these ... \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  leading the losses among emerging markets," \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  analyst Thu Lan Nguyen said.\par \par \uc2 The lira and rand traded at four- and five-month lows against the dollar, but weakened to a lesser extent than their central European peers.\par \par \uc2 Poland also enjoyed strong demand at an auction of five-year bonds, though analysts attributed this mostly to local buying.\par \par \uc2 Emerging sovereign bonds' yield spreads over U.S. Treasuries widened to 3-1/2-month highs of 389 basis points and the cost of insuring exposure to emerging credits rose sharply, with Polish, Russian and Turkish credit default swaps at four-month highs, according to Markit data.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Drazen Jorgic and Carolyn Cohn; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING (UPDATE 1) | ABX | BNX | FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120519e85g0003n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
