\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 India Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Likely  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  To Support Rupee - Dealers\b0\par\par\uc2 536 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2012\par 08:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely sold dollars from INR54.13, say dealers\par \par \uc2 -- Dollar drops to INR53.64, but recoups some losses as demand remains high\par \par \uc2 -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and administrative steps unlikely to change rupee outlook, says analyst\par \par \uc2 (Updates market level in 3rd paragraph; adds comments in 6th, 8th 9th, 11th paragraphs.)\par \par \uc2 By Sourav Mishra and Sudeep Jain\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets early Tuesday to prop up the rupee, dealers said, after the local unit came close to its all-time low against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  likely started selling dollars when the greenback hit INR54.13, not far from its all-time high of INR54.2925 recorded On Dec. 15, three dealers told Dow Jones Newswires.\par \par \uc2 After the suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar fell to an intraday low of INR53.64. However, the dollar recouped some of its losses and was last trading at INR53.87, indicating sustained demand for the greenback.\par \par \uc2 An RBI spokeswoman was unavailable for comment.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't say whether or not it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and has a stated policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  only to curb volatility.\par \par \uc2 The RBI's suspected presence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets over the past few sessions is evidence of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strong discomfort with the trajectory of the rupee, said analysts.\par \par \uc2 The RBI's room to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  is limited by \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves--currently $293.2 billion--which is modest given the country's trade deficit of $185 billion in the last fiscal year ended March 31.\par \par \uc2 Market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the RBI's recent administrative measures such as the move to force exporters to sell half of their foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings are unlikely to turn the tide for the rupee, said analysts.\par \par \uc2 India's stubborn inflation, below-trend growth and the rupee's depreciation are essentially manifestations of the underlying economic imbalances due to "a combination of policy incoherence, shifting global risk appetite and a comatose government," said Rajeev Malik, senior economist at CLSA in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 Foreign fund inflows have fallen sharply in recent weeks following the government's proposal to change India's laws to target tax avoidance. New Delhi's move last week to postpone the implementation of the new tax rule by a year has done little to improve sentiment.\par \par \uc2 Standard Chartered Bank estimates foreign investors have pulled out $1.3 billion from Indian stocks and bonds since the tax measures were proposed in March.\par \par \uc2 The government's record on promoting foreign direct investment has also been poor. Late last year, a much-anticipated move allowing multi-brand foreign retailers to hold a 51% stake in Indian ventures was rolled back in the face of stiff political opposition.\par \par \uc2 These setbacks have exacerbated concerns over India's wide fiscal and current account deficits and made the rupee vulnerable to bouts of risk aversion sparked by troubles in the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 -By Sourav Mishra and Sudeep Jain, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 6145 6123; sudeep.jain@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 15, 2012 02:28 ET (06:28 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120515e85f001hh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
