\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ  \highlight22\uc2 India Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Adviser: Market  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  By RBI Won't Arrest Rupee Slide\b0\par\par\uc2 450 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2012\par 12:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 15 May 2012 06:24 EDT *DJ  RBI Adviser: Wide Current Account Gap At The Heart Of Rupee Problems\par \par \uc2 15 May 2012 06:25 EDT *DJ  RBI Adviser: Rupee Fall Serious, Govt Must Raise Fuel Prices To Cut Current Account Gap\par \par \uc2 15 May 2012 06:25 EDT *DJ  RBI Adviser: Raising Fuel Prices To Also Help Restore Confidence, Attract Inflows\par \par \uc2 15 May 2012 06:26 EDT *DJ  RBI Has Limited Options Left To Check Rupee Fall, Onus On Govt To Act -Adviser\par \par \uc2 15 May 2012 06:26 EDT *DJ  RBI Adviser: \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Reserves Limited, Shouldn't Blow Them Away\par \par \uc2 15 May 2012 06:26 EDT *DJ  RBI Adviser: Must Anchor Expectations Rupee Won't Go On Depreciating\par \par \uc2 15 May 2012 06:42 EDT DJ  RBI Has Few Options Left To Check Rupee's Fall, Govt Must Step In - Adviser\par \par \uc2 NEW DELHI (Dow Jones)--The recent frequent market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't arrest the rupee's slide and the government must raise fuel prices to cut the country's ballooning current account deficit, a top adviser to the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The current account deficit is at the heart of India's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  problems, Sudipto Mundle, a member of the RBI's technical advisory committee on monetary policy, told Dow Jones Newswires.\par \par \uc2 He added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  now has few options left, and the government must step in.\par \par \uc2 "The government of the day needs to have the guts to do this [raise fuel prices]," he said.\par \par \uc2 "If they don't, no matter what the RBI does, you are not going to get out of this problem."\par \par \uc2 Mundle's comments come at a time the Indian rupee has weakened close to its all-time lows as the country's current account deficit widens to its highest in several years. Foreign fund inflows have slowed due to fading investor confidence.\par \par \uc2 Earlier Tuesday, the dollar rose to the day's high of INR54.13, not far from its record high of INR54.29, before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sold dollars.\par \par \uc2 The greenback was last trading at INR53.75.\par \par \uc2 India's fiscal deficit widened to 5.9% of gross domestic product in the fiscal year ended March 31, overshooting the budget estimate of 4.6% because of heavy subsidies on fuels, fertilizers and food.\par \par \uc2 The budget deficit could exceed the target this year as well unless the government raises fuel prices.\par \par \uc2 --By Anant Vijay Kala, Dow Jones Newswires; +91-11-43563311; anant.kala@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 15, 2012 06:42 ET (10:42 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120515e85f0032d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
