\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  GLOBAL CALL: Our Take On The Day's Big  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  News\b0\par\par\uc2 556 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2012\par 13:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Global Call covers the main talking points from an 11:00 GMT news meeting involving DJ \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trader editors in New York, London and Singapore, as well as other \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  hot spots when warranted.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     By Brian Baskin \par     Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1. The latest development in Greece's post-election drama helped stabilize many \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that had sold off sharply Monday. Greece is to pay out EUR450 million in foreign law bonds not covered by the restructuring deal. While expected, the news helps reassure investors that this debt won't turn into another time bomb. Less promising was a 6.2% annual contraction in first-quarter GDP and the growing possibility of a do-over election June 17.\par \par \uc2 2. Elsewhere in Europe, the data were mixed. The euro zone as a whole avoided recession, with GDP flat in the first quarter. That small victory rested entirely on Germany's shoulders, after the country's economy grew 0.5% from the fourth quarter. We're still seeing the divergence between Europe's stronger and weaker economies, with recession gripping Greece, Spain and even the Netherlands, while Germany, Austria and a handful of others hold up better than expected.\par \par \uc2 3. Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have taken a huge hit since the Greek elections, and we're starting to see central banks react: a. The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the rupee once again, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  approached a record low against the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has shown it's willing to fight, but with relatively low foreign reserves, it may be running out of ammo. b. Korea's finance minister called recent moves in the won excessive, the first hint in some time that the normally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 -happy country is considering action to support its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The won has fallen for five straight sessions, hitting a four-month low against the dollar. c. Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't stepped in to halt the real's slide, even as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plunged past the BRL1.9798 against the dollar level where the market was certain an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be triggered. The real is now around 2 to the dollar, and with inflation already a concern for policy makers, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely a matter of when, not if.\par \par \uc2 4. The \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  released minutes from its May 1 meeting, where it cut a key interest rate by 50 basis points, double market expectations. There was little new insight into the decision--it was made to give mortgage holders a break and help the economy, as we already knew. More interesting was the Treasury Secretary's comments separately Tuesday, where the RBA board member hinted there is room for more rate cuts this year. The Australian dollar is back above $1 after dropping below that key level for the first time since Dec. 20 on Monday.\par \par \uc2 5. Foreign direct investment in China fell by 0.7% in April, the sixth consecutive decline. A commerce ministry spokesperson also said to expect the country's trade surplus to shrink again.\par \par \uc2 (Brian Baskin is assistant managing editor for the Americas at DJ \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trader, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  news service jointly produced by Dow Jones Newswires and The Wall Street Journal.) [ 15-05-12 1118GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020120515e85f0000m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
