\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indian rupee bounces from near record low; RBI steps in\b0\par\par\uc2 423 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2012\par 05:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Adds quotes, details, levels)\par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, May 15 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee strengthened sharply on Tuesday from a near record low against the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in with what dealers called "massive" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , signalling an intent to defend the beleaguered domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  is believed to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively this month as the rupee moved steadily towards its all-time low driven by a mixture of worsening global risk aversion and concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fiscal and economic challenges.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been accompanied by surprise measures such as forcing exporters to convert half of their foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their accounts. \par \par \uc2  Besides, the RBI announced on Monday it would purchase bonds via open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the end of the week, its second weekly OMO, which analysts widely interpret as intended to offset the impact on rupee liquidity from its dollar sales.\par \par \uc2  "RBI will keep up the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  though ongoing Greek impasse and broad dollar strength will keep USD/INR biased for gains," said Radhika Rao, an economist at Forecast Pte in Singapore, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will defend the 54 rupees per dollar level.\par \par \uc2  "As a backstop to alleviate liquidity strain, OMOs could become more frequent."\par \par \uc2  The Indian rupee dropped as low as 54.15 to the dollar soon after the day's opening trade, not far from a record low of 54.30 to the dollar hit in mid-December. It closed at  53.9750 on Monday.\par \par \uc2  However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was soon seen stepping in with dollar sales via state-run banks, s harply pushing down USD/INR, which was last trading at 53.85/8650 after hitting as low as 53.50.\par \par \uc2  "It seems like a massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a chief dealer with a state-run bank said.\par \par \uc2  The OMO announcement sent bond yields lower, with the benchmark 2021 bond yield down 4 basis points at  8.48 percent.\par \par \uc2  Analysts are split about whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can continue to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but in the near term, they say the RBI is looking to keep USD/INR below 54.\par \par \uc2  "RBI's action was very clear and concerted. It won't tolerate rupee weakness beyond 54.30 levels, possibly even 54 levels," said Subramanian Sharma, director at Greenback \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Archana Narayanan and Subhadip Sircar; Writing by Rafael Nam; editing by Malini Menon)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA/RUPEE (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | M | RBN | SNI | SNS | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120518e85f00056\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
