\par\par \b \uc2 Indian Shares End Up After Five Sessions On Bargain Buying In Blue Chips\b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2012\par 13:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--Indian shares rose Tuesday, ending five sessions of losses, on the back of bargain-buying by investors who picked up blue chips like \uc2 Larsen & Toubro\uc2  and \uc2 Infosys\uc2  and as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  managed to check the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bombay Stock Exchange\uc2 's 30-stock Sensitive Index rose 112.41 points, or 0.7%, to end at 16,328.25, after trading between 16,123.04 and 16,370.12 during the session.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark still remains down 4.5% for the last one month.\par \par \uc2 The National Stock Exchange's 50-stock Nifty index rose 35.00 points, or 0.7%, to close at 4,942.80.\par \par \uc2 Trading volume in the BSE's cash segment fell to INR17.88 billion from Monday's INR18.04 billion. Advancers outnumbered decliners 1,365 to 1,329, while 132 stocks remained unchanged.\par \par \uc2 "The stock markets were in a heavily oversold position and there is some consolidation in stock prices at the current levels," said P.S. Balasubramanian, head of institutional business at \uc2 Vertex Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A Hong Kong-based hedge-fund manager, declining to be named, said Indian shares looked good bargains for foreign funds after their prices fell sharply over the last month and due to the dollar's gains against the Indian rupee. "There is some bargain-buying but no serious fresh investment flows" into Indian shares, he added.\par \par \uc2 The rupee has been in a free-fall against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, a likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market supported the rupee. The dollar was at INR53.77 in afternoon trade, off the day's high of INR54.11.\par \par \uc2 Engineering and construction major \uc2 Larsen & Toubro\uc2  ended 5.4% up at INR1,222.50, a day after it reported strong quarterly results.\par \par \uc2 Infosys\uc2  rose 3.1% to INR2,411.20 after \uc2 Ashok Vemuri\uc2 , head of its U.S. business, told Dow Jones Newswires that the company is seeing early signs of business picking up in the U.S.--its largest market--although clients remain cautious of investing in information technology services in an uncertain environment.\par \par \uc2 Among the losers, \uc2 Bharti Airtel\uc2  fell 1.3% to INR303.50 after Junior Finance Minister S.S. Palanimanickam told parliament that the Directorate of Enforcement is investigating charges of money laundering and violations of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules against the company. He declined to elaborate, citing ongoing investigations.\par \par \uc2 -By Raghavendra Upadhyaya; Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 61456103; raghavendra.upadhyaya@dowjones.com [ 15-05-12 1105GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5064 55106   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120515e85f00132\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
