\par\par \b \uc2 MARKETS WRAP-Indian rupee drops to near 54; bonds gain\b0\par\par\uc2 678 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 2012\par 08:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Indian rupee closes at record closing low of 53.96/97\par \par \uc2  * Stocks drop on global risk aversion; domestic inflation\par \par \uc2  * Bond yields fall; liquidity measures eyed \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2  By Archana Narayanan and Subhadip Sircar\par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, May 14 (Reuters) - India's rupee dropped to a record closing low on Monday, while bond prices gained in a volatile session marked by a sharp rise in global risk aversion and higher-than-expected domestic inflation data that reduced expectations for monetary easing.\par \par \uc2  The uncertainty sparked by the aftermath of Greek elections and concerns about China's economy are exposing the vulnerability of Indian markets at a time of deep concerns over the country's economy and its fiscal standing. \par \par \uc2  Foreign outflows have been a particular concern, in light of a current account deficit that reached 4.3 percent of gross domestic product as of the December quarter. \par \par \uc2  Clouding the picture further, data on Monday showed wholesale price inflation for April rose to 7.23 percent, above expectations, at a time when economic growth has slumped to a near three-year low. \par \par \uc2  However, analysts said the data was at least tempered by the more muted gains seen in core inflation, while markets could see support should the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and buying bonds.\par \par \uc2  "If we see more softening in core prices, the headroom for the RBI to support growth more is likely to expand, especially after the recent weak production numbers," said Siddhartha Sanyal, chief India economist at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, is still somewhat cautious about inflation and the potential impact of more rate cuts on inflation expectations."\par \par \uc2  After a strong start in January and February, Indian markets have tumbled, which many analysts attribute to a poorly-received fiscal budget unveiled in mid-March as well as a controversial set of taxation proposals for foreign investors.\par \par \uc2  The government's fiscal standing and a perception of slowing policy reforms remain key risks, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's response will also be critical for the outlook in markets.\par \par \uc2  Though few analysts expect the RBI to cut interest rates at its policy meeting next month, analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could at least seek to tackle a severe cash crunch via open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  or a cut in the cash reserve ratio.\par \par \uc2  Those liquidity hopes helped benchmark 2021 bonds, with yields falling 4 basis points to 8.52 percent, and by expectations for a new benchmark bond to be sold at Friday's auction.\par \par \uc2  After the markets' close, the RBI said it would buy up to 120 billion rupees of debt on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The 1-year OIS rate ended unchanged at 8.04 percent, while the 5-year OIS rate fell 3 bps at 7.48 percent after the data.\par \par \uc2  "Core inflation is still below 5 percent, so the data does not change policy expectations much," said Sandeep Bagla, executive vice-president at ICICI Securities Primary Dealership Ltd, referring to WPI.\par \par \uc2  "We expect liquidity infusion measures to continue."\par \par \uc2  In stocks, India's main BSE index dropped to its lowest close since Jan. 16, tracking a sharp fall in European shares. \par \par \uc2  Banks such as \uc2 HDFC Bank\uc2  led decliners, in a session also marked by the momentary stop in the execution of orders of Nifty futures in the National Stock Exchange.\par \par \uc2  The rupee dropped to a record closing low of 53.96/97 to the dollar, very close to breaching the psychologically key 54-level and not far from the record low of 54.30 hit in mid-December.\par \par \uc2  The falls came despite suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the afternoon.\par \par \uc2  The one-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts\par \par \uc2 were at 53.95, while the most-traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and the United Stock Exchange all ended around 54.12 on a total volume of 4.4 billion. \par \par \uc2 (Writing by Rafael Nam)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA/WPI (UPDATE 1) | ABN | E | RBN | SNI | SNS | M | D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120514e85e000n9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
