\par\par \b \uc2 India Shares End Down On Inflation Worries; Larsen Gains On Earnings\b0\par\par\uc2 475 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 2012\par 13:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--Indian shares fell Monday, as higher-than-expected inflation numbers damped hopes of any immediate rate cut by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and as continuing political worries over Europe weighed on sentiment.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bombay Stock Exchange\uc2 's 30-stock Sensitive Index slipped 77.14 points, or 0.5%, to end at 16,215.84, its lowest finish since Jan. 16. The index traded between 16,124.82 and 16,390 during the session.\par \par \uc2 The National Stock Exchange's 50-stock Nifty declined 21.10 points, or 0.4%, to close at 4,907.80.\par \par \uc2 Trading volume in the BSE's cash segment fell to INR18.04 billion from Friday's INR18.93 billion. Decliners outnumbered gainers 1,657 to 1,047, while 117 stocks remained unchanged.\par \par \uc2 "Things are really bad, and investors are losing hope in the stock markets. Even good corporate results are discounted in the spate of negative news on the economy," said Vijay Kedia, director at Kedia Securities.\par \par \uc2 The April inflation reading at 7.23%--versus a 6.67% rise estimated in a Dow Jones Newswires poll--and the falling rupee have led to concerns of a resurgence in price increases, making it difficult for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease monetary policy and support faltering growth.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt a sharp slide in the rupee against the U.S. dollar failed to bring much cheer to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the stock market. The dollar was at INR53.80 as of 1004 GMT after the suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , down from an intraday high of INR53.91 and compared with INR53.63 late Friday in Asia. The rupee's all-time low against the dollar is 54.2925, which it touched on Dec. 15.\par \par \uc2 Banks were the major losers, on fears that without further cuts in interest rates, the sector may suffer from muted loan growth and high bad loans.\par \par \uc2 The BSE Bankex index fell 1.6%, with \uc2 ICICI Bank\uc2  declining 1.7% to close at INR799.10. \uc2 HDFC Bank\uc2  slid 2% to end at INR500.50.\par \par \uc2 Engineering and construction major \uc2 Larsen & Toubro\uc2  ended up 1.8% at INR1,159.80 after its net profit for the fiscal fourth quarter through March rose a better-than-expected 14%, driven by a strong order backlog.\par \par \uc2 Heavyweight Reliance Industries closed 2.3% lower at INR681.15. Moody's Investors Service said earlier in the day that the cut by \uc2 Reliance Industries\uc2  in its proved gas reserves estimate is credit negative for the company as it confirms the technical difficulties the energy major faces in the exploration and production business from declining output and lower cash flows.\par \par \uc2 -By Raghavendra Upadhyaya, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 61456103; raghavendra.upadhyaya@dowjones.com [ 14-05-12 1102GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5064 55106   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120514e85e0012n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
