\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupee, Sing dlr up on c.banks but Europe weighs on other units\b0\par\par\uc2 896 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2012\par 07:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * RBI curbs exporters \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings to lift rupee\par \par \uc2 * Sing dlr gains on local bids, wary of c.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Won dips; exporters, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  caution relive\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, May 10 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee led gains among emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took dramatic regulatory measures to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the Singapore dollar rose amid expectations of an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by authorities.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI)\uc2 , tightening the rules on exporters earnings, asked them to reduce their foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings by half, effectively forcing them to buy the rupee .\par \par \uc2 It also raised the intraday open position trading band to five times the available net position limit for banks, in a move to improve liquidity.\par \par \uc2 The measures helped the rupee jump up to 1.6 percent against the dollar, but it gave up some of gains as the impact of the steps was seen temporary, given India's growing current account deficit.\par \par \uc2 The rupee has been the worst performer among \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in emerging Asia after the Indonesian rupiah, falling to its lowest level earlier this month since December.\par \par \uc2 Other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in emerging Asia were also under pressure as weak Chinese trade data and political uncertainty in the euro zone stoked renewed fears of a global slowdown.\par \par \uc2 "Greek worries and China data are expected to keep weighing on emerging Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Also there is growing evidence of slowing growth in the region as well. They will be supportive of USD/Asia to trend higher from here," said Enrico Tanuwidjaja, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Maybank in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 Some regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  found relief from better-than-expected Australia's jobs data and on expectations that central banks in the area may step in to defend the units.\par \par \uc2 The Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted buying the rupiah , dealers said. Others warned r egulatory measures such as RBI's steps could only have limited impact.\par \par \uc2 "While this kind of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the short-term, it is actually a negative for investor confidence," said Frances Cheung, senior strategist for \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2  CIB in Hong Kong. "Other policymakers will be very cautious in considering such restrictions."\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 U.S. dollar/Singapore dollar fell as traders grew cautious about a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 There was market talk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's agent banks may have sold the pair at 1.2550 overnight.\par \par \uc2 It also came under pressure from strong Australia's jobs data and a rebound in the euro.\par \par \uc2 Resistance stood at a 55-day moving average of 1.2535.\par \par \uc2 RINGGIT\par \par \uc2 Dollar/ringgit slid on the euro's rebound and Australia's jobs data, but it found support around a 100-day moving average at 3.0651.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday the pair ended higher than the average for the first time since mid-January.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, it rose to 3.0750, the highest since April 12, breaking through a 76.4 percent Fibonacci retracement of its March-May slide.\par \par \uc2 But short-term speculators took profits, capping its rally.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 Dollar/won initially hit a near four-month high as worries about European politics bolstered risk aversion.\par \par \uc2 But South Korean exporters sold the pair on rallies, prompting stop-loss dollar selling, while investors stayed cautious over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities, limiting its gains.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  investors largely ignored the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to leave rates unchanged as it was widely expected.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Change on the day at 0720 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        79.75          79.64       -0.14\par  Sing dlr        1.2482         1.2531       +0.39\par  Taiwan dlr      29.349         29.400       +0.17\par  Korean won     1141.70        1140.40       -0.11\par  Baht             31.05          31.08       +0.10\par  Peso             42.39          42.41       +0.05\par  Rupiah         9245.00        9225.00       -0.22\par  Rupee            53.31          53.82       +0.96\par  Ringgit         3.0615         3.0695       +0.26\par  Yuan            6.3124         6.3097       -0.04\par  Change so far in 2012\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \hi