\par\par \b \uc2 India Sets  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Restrictions To Curb Rupee's Fall\b0\par\par\uc2 674 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2012\par 09:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unveils steps to counter the rupee's decline\par \par \uc2 -- Analysts say the measures will provide temporary support but won't reverse the rupee's trend\par \par \uc2 -- Foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earners must convert 50% of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  into rupees within two weeks\par \par \uc2 -- Banks' intraday position limits set at five times overnight limit\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI -- India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday moved aggressively to halt a sharp slide in the rupee, imposing \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions on companies and tightening trading rules for banks, but analysts said the measures may not be enough to reverse the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trend.\par \par \uc2 The move marks a stepped-up effort to put a floor under the rupee after a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in recent days failed to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's losses.\par \par \uc2 The announcement boosted the beleaguered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sending the dollar down to an intraday low of INR52.94 compared to INR53.82 late Wednesday in Asia. That bounce may soon fade, however, with India's large current account and budget deficits and entrenched inflation continuing to undercut the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The RBI is getting into micromanagement of the market but fundamental problems such as the fiscal and current account deficit remain," said Moses Harding, head of the global markets group at \uc2 IndusInd Bank\uc2 . The decision to resort to such piecemeal steps indicates the RBI is running out of ammunition to protect the rupee, he said.\par \par \uc2 The RBI said in a statement that all \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  earners -- including exporters -- have to convert 50% of the total \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings kept in banks into rupees. This must be done within two weeks.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said companies will now be allowed to keep only 50% of their total \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings in their Exchange Earners' Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Accounts and that they will have to convert the rest into rupees. The EEFC accounts allow exporters to hold foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in onshore accounts for imports and other expenses.\par \par \uc2 In addition, companies will have to draw down their EEFC accounts fully before they buy any \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the RBI said. The measures are also applicable to foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  accounts of resident Indians and so-called Diamond Dollar Accounts held by diamond exporters.\par \par \uc2 The RBI also sought to reduce speculation against the rupee, with a separate move that fixed banks' intra-day open position limits at five times their net overnight open position limit.\par \par \uc2 The new limits are lower than the previous limits, which the RBI had individually specified for banks, three traders told Dow Jones Newswires. Open positions are unhedged \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say the measures will increase the supply of dollars in the market and provide temporary support to the rupee, which was headed toward its record low of 54.2925 to the dollar that it hit on Dec. 15.\par \par \uc2 The measures follow a series of steps the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has taken in recent months to shore up the rupee.\par \par \uc2 Since December, the RBI has banned the cancellation and rebooking of forward contracts with the same underlying exposure and made it easier for companies to avail foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans. It has also freed interest rates on rupee accounts held by overseas Indians and those on export credit and increased the interest-rate ceiling on onshore foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  accounts held by overseas Indians.\par \par \uc2 The Indian rupee has borne the brunt of sharp fall in capital inflows in recent weeks due to concerns over proposed changes to India's tax laws. These have exacerbated jitters over India's wide fiscal deficit and the current account deficit which Asia's third-largest economy runs due to perennial trade gap.\par \par \uc2 The trade gap for the last fiscal year ended March 31 was $184.9 billion whereas India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are less than $300 billion, leaving the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  little room to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to protect the rupee.\par \par \uc2 - By Sudeep Jain, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 6145 6123; sudeep.jain@dowjones. om [ 05-10-12 0335ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020120510e85a0002b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
