\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee drops on fears of continued outflows\b0\par\par\uc2 402 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2012\par 13:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  as USD/INR gains to 54-levels\par \par \uc2 * USD/INR's record high of 54.30 could be hit-traders\par \par \uc2 * Rupee starting to look fundamentally attractive-analyst\par \par \uc2 By Subhadip Sircar\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 9 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee suffered its biggest percentage fall in nearly five months against the dollar on Wednesday as investors pull out of global risky assets, sparking a new round of suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors have sold a net of nearly 10 billion rupees ($187.88 million) of domestic equities in the previous two sessions, as political uncertainty in Greece combines with continued worries about taxation for investments from overseas.\par \par \uc2 The falls prompted suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the rupee fell around the 53.80 levels to the dollar, according to five dealers.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is believed to have been active selling dollars in the past few sessions whenever the rupee approaches the psychologically key 54.00 level.\par \par \uc2 "I think the RBI will be actively protecting the 53.80/90 levels," said Hemal Doshi, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Geojit Comtrade.\par \par \uc2 The rupee fell 1.36 percent against the dollar to 53.82/83, its biggest daily percentage loss since Dec. 12. It had closed at 53.12/13 on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Despite the RBI's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders warn the rupee could soon surpass a record low of 54.30 hit in December.\par \par \uc2 India remains buffeted by the twin deficits on the external account and fiscal side, leaving it vulnerable to volatile capital inflows to plug its balance of payments.\par \par \uc2 However, to some analysts, the sharp falls in the rupee are making its valuations more alluring.\par \par \uc2 "These factors make the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fundamentally attractive and recent positive policy moves suggest that the timing to buy the INR looks right," \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2  said in a note.\par \par \uc2 It expects the rupee to trade at 50 to the dollar by end-2012.\par \par \uc2 The one-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts\par \par \uc2 were at 54.18.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most-traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and the United Stock Exchange all ended around 54.0625 on a total volume of $5.42 billion. ($1 = 53.2250 Indian rupees)\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Rafael Nam)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA/RUPEE | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | SNI | SNS | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120512e8590005a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
