\par\par \b \uc2 Indian Rupee Down Despite Likely RBI  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Fall\b0\par\par\uc2 514 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2012\par 14:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                     At 1200 GMT \par                          Latest      Change \par    USD/INR                53.82      +0.70 \par    9.15% 2024 Bond        8.59       +2 BPs \par    Call Rate              8.37%      -3 BPs \par    Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par    April                  3.05       -0.01 \par    *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount are midpoints of bid-offer spreads \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee tumbled against the dollar Wednesday, despite a suspected market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as persistent uncertainty in the euro zone, demand for the greenback from oil importers and weak sentiment on the country's fiscal health roiled investors.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The dollar in late trade was at INR53.82, a tad off its intraday high of INR53.83 and compared with INR53.12 late Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to sell dollars at around INR53.80, pulling the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down to INR53.69, three dealers told Dow Jones Newswires. However, the last half an hour of trade again saw a buying spree pushing the dollar up.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't give details of its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It seems like an over-reaction which has surprised us all," said Ananth Narayan G, regional head for fixed income, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and commodities at Standard Chartered Bank.\par \par \uc2 The dollar in the near term, technically, may test its all-time high of INR54.295, but fundamentally the outlook looks over-pessimistic and the pair should settle below INR53.00, he said, adding that capital inflows into the stock market will have a major role to play.\par \par \uc2 Pramit Brahmbhatt of Alpari \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said the rupee's sharp fall was more a work of "sentiments." He expects a likely correction in the level by the end of this month or in early June.\par \par \uc2 In the government bonds market, profit-taking following a strong rally Tuesday brought down the prices even as traders look forward to the March industrial production data and bond auctions.\par \par \uc2 The most-traded 9.15% 2024 bond ended at INR104.23, compared with INR104.40 Tuesday, while the benchmark 8.79% 2021 paper finished at INR101.47 from its previous close of INR101.60.\par \par \uc2 Bond prices had gained Tuesday after the RBI earlier this week announced a bond buyback of up to INR120 billion Friday. It will also sell four bonds of INR150 billion on the same day.\par \par \uc2 "We expect the bonds to be trading in a range ahead of the crucial data print and the bond sale. However, we expect the 10-year note to see bearish cutoffs," a senior dealer at a state-run bank said.\par \par \uc2 Trading interest in the benchmark paper is fading as the market expects the RBI to soon replace it with a new 10-year paper.\par \par \uc2 India's industrial production growth in March likely grew 1.5% from a year earlier in March, after rising 4.1% in February, according to the median estimate in a Dow Jones Newswires poll of 14 economists.\par \par \uc2 -By Nupur Acharya; Dow Jones Newswires; +91-22-61456117; nupur.acharya@dowjones.com [ 09-05-12 1254GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120509e859001bk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict