\par\par \b \uc2 India  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2 's Gokarn: Pressures On Food Inflation Still Very Strong\b0\par\par\uc2 197 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2012\par 08:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Asian Equities Report\par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 HYDERABAD, India (Dow Jones)--India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has relatively little room to cut interest rates now, Deputy Governor Subir Gokarn said Tuesday, reiterating guidance given in April.\par \par \uc2 He pointed to inflation, and said there is a risk that it could accelerate again, given that oil prices remain high.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  is conscious also of the recent volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements, and it has direct and administrative tools to deal with the issue, Gokarn said at a conference.\par \par \uc2 His comments come at a time when the Indian rupee has partially recovered after touching a near five-month low last week. It was last trading at 53.02 to the dollar.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't give details of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and has a stated policy of getting into the market only to control volatility.\par \par \uc2 At its April policy review, the RBI slashed rates by a sharper-than-expected half a percentage point, but said that there is limited scope for more cuts.\par \par \uc2 --By Khushita Vasant, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 6145 6123; sudeep.jain@dowjones.com [ 08-05-12 0727GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument AER0000020120508e8580001g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
