\par\par \b \uc2 Indian Rupee Recovers From Near 5-Month Low On Likely RBI  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Fall\b0\par\par\uc2 491 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Mai 2012\par 14:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par                     At 1200 GMT \par                          Latest      Change \par    USD/INR                53.47      +0.06 \par    9.15% 2024 Bond        8.69%      +4 BPs \par    Call Rate              8.25%      -8 BPs \par    Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par    April                  3.1050     -0.08 \par    *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount are midpoints of bid-offer spreads \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee recouped most of its intraday losses Friday on the back of heavy suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the local unit came perilously close to its record low against the U.S. dollar, dealers said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  likely sold dollars on a large scale on at least two occasions starting from when the greenback was trading at INR53.88, four dealers told Dow Jones Newswires.\par \par \uc2 An RBI spokeswoman wasn't available for comment.\par \par \uc2 The suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped lift the rupee from an intraday low of 53.91 to the dollar--its lowest level since the all-time low of 54.2925 it hit on Dec. 15. The dollar was at INR53.47 in late Asian trade, compared with INR53.41 late Thursday.\par \par \uc2 But, analysts say the rupee's downward trend can't be reversed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , whose capacity to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  is limited due to \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dwindling \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. In addition, any sale of dollars or purchase of rupees by the RBI risks aggravating the cash crunch in the local banking system.\par \par \uc2 "The RBI's options are severely limited, and it alone can't manage this problem. We need some policy measures that will bring in more flows," said Partha Mukherjee, president of treasury and international banking at \uc2 Axis Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rupee had gained as much as 9% against the greenback earlier this year. But, concerns over proposed changes to India's tax laws, coupled with India's weak economic fundamentals, have sparked a flight of foreign capital in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 Capital flows are an important source of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  to plug India's gaping current account deficit, which the economy runs due to a perennial trade gap.\par \par \uc2 "India's high dependence on risk-driven volatile capital inflows makes it like a global risk on/off fireball," CLSA said in a note.\par \par \uc2 In the sovereign-debt markets, bonds fell sharply after an INR180 billion auction received poor demand.\par \par \uc2 The most-traded 9.15% 2024 bond ended at INR103.43, down from INR103.78 at Thursday's close. The cutoff yield for the 9.15% 2024 bond came in at 8.72%, against the median estimate of 8.64% in a Dow Jones Newsires poll of five dealers.\par \par \uc2 Bond prices and yields move in opposite directions, and higher-than-expected yield cutoffs at an auction indicate that buyers were unwilling to pay higher prices for the bonds.\par \par \uc2 - By Sudeep Jain, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 6145 6123; sudeep.jain@dowjones.com [ 04-05-12 1232GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120504e854000sp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
