\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee drops, sparking suspected RBI action\b0\par\par\uc2 430 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Mai 2012\par 08:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupee falls below 53, to near 4-month low\par \par \uc2 * RBI likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend rupee-dealers\par \par \uc2 * More rupee falls seen; RBI has limited firepower\par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2 By Subhadip Sircar\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 2 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee dipped below 53 to the dollar on Wednesday, nearly touching a four-month low, as oil importers bought the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped it recoup some losses.\par \par \uc2 Though the rupee is likely to continue facing strong support at the 53 level in the near-term, traders expect further falls, given India's fiscal and economic challenges, and fears that waning foreign flows will worsen the current account deficit.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, dealers say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has limited firepower to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  should the rupee continue to fall, given dollar sales would exacerbate an acute liquidity crunch in India's banking system.\par \par \uc2 Economists also say India's relatively modest \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves -- with the lowest import cover since 1996 according to a recent Bank of America-Merrill Lynch report -- do not provide enough ammunition for a strong defense of the rupee.\par \par \uc2 "The RBI was not so aggressive in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They also feel that the rupee should weaken given the macroeconomic fundamentals. They will only cap the volatility," said Hemal Doshi, chief financial strategist at Geojit Comtrade.\par \par \uc2 The rupee fell to a low of 53.02 to the dollar on Wednesday, a level last seen on Jan 5, before pulling back to close at 52.96/97 levels. It had closed at 52.73/74 on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Four dealers said that state-run banks were seen selling dollars when the rupee broke below 53, which they said was likely on behalf of the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some dealers said the RBI also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the rupee forwards market to offset the liquidity impact of its spot selling.\par \par \uc2 "There were rumours of RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in spot market through nationalised banks and simultaneous action in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards and bonds to neutralize the impact on money market liquidity," said Paresh Nayar, head of fixed income and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at First Rand Bank.\par \par \uc2 The one-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts\par \par \uc2 were at 53.32.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most-traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and the United Stock Exchange all ended around 53.26 on a total volume of $4 billion.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Archana Narayan; Editing by Rafael Nam)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA/RUPEE (UPDATE 2) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | SNI | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120505e8520002m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
