\par\par \b \uc2 REFILE-Indian rupee falls for 4th week; bearish bets pile up\b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2012\par 15:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Refiles to fix typo in first paragraph)\par \par \uc2 * S&P outlook cut hurts rupee for the week\par \par \uc2 * Bearish bets pile up on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * No RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  til USD/INR hits 54-analyst\par \par \uc2 By Subhadip Sircar\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, April 27 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee posted a fourth consecutive week of falls after ending flat on Friday, as investors add more bearish bets on a local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that is pricing in deep uncertainties about the country's economic and fiscal challenges.\par \par \uc2 Those challenges were most recently highlighted by \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2 , which downgraded India's outlook to negative this week, in the latest negative development impacting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The weakening rupee has led to talk of potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but traders believe that is unlikely given the country's modest \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and tight liquidity conditions.\par \par \uc2 "Looking at the current account deficit and the reserve situation, I do not think that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling reserves," said Abhishek Goenka, chief executive at \b \highlight22\uc2 India Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Advisors.\par \par \uc2 He said that the rupee may fall as much as 54 to the dollar before any \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It had hit a life-low of 54.30 in mid-December.\par \par \uc2 The rupee settled flat at 52.54/55 to the dollar against 52.55/56 on Thursday. It fell nearly 1 percent for the week.\par \par \uc2 Friday's trading was mostly rangebound with the USD/INR oscillating in a 52.47-52.73 band.\par \par \uc2 India is buffeted by twin current account and fiscal deficits, which added to slowing policy reforms and relatively high inflation, is making for a potentially toxic mix.\par \par \uc2 A Reuters poll on Thursday showed market players had nearly doubled short Indian rupee bets, largest since November.\par \par \uc2 The one-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts\par \par \uc2 were at 52.90.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most-traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and the United Stock Exchange all ended around 52.88 on a total volume of $2.6 billion.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA/RUPEE (UPDATE 1) (CORRECTED) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | SNI | SNS | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120430e84r000tl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
