\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  Rupee Off Over 15-Week Low On RBI  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Steady\b0\par\par\uc2 445 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 April 2012\par 14:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          At 1200 GMT \par                          Latest      Change \par    USD/INR                52.68      +0.18 \par    8.79% 2021 Bond        8.57%      Unchanged \par    Call Rate              8.40%      +9BPs \par    Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par    Mar                    3.050      +0.030 \par    *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount are midpoints of bid-offer spreads \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee recovered some of its losses after dropping to a more than 15-week low against the U.S. dollar Tuesday, after a likely \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  toward the close of trade in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  likely sold dollars when the greenback was trading at INR52.78, three dealers told Dow Jones Newswires.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was last trading at INR52.68, off its intraday high of INR52.87, a level last seen Jan. 6.\par \par \uc2 The suspected RBI action comes as the rupee has resumed its downward trend against the dollar after having gained as much as 8% in the early part of 2012.\par \par \uc2 "Trade and current account deficits are widening, euro zone concerns are back again and there are lesser capital inflows into local stocks, which will keep the rupee weak," said K. Harihar, treasurer at \uc2 FirstRand Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Harihar said INR53.40 will be the crucial resistance level for the dollar in the near term.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said firm local stocks also aided in some recovery during session.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bombay Stock Exchange\uc2 's 30-stock Sensitive Index rose 0.7% to end at 17,207.29.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Indian government bonds ended steady Monday as some value buying at lower levels limited concerns of heavy supplies during the week and expected inflationary pressures.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark 8.79% 2021 bond ended at INR101.43, compared with INR101.42 Monday.\par \par \uc2 The Indian government Tuesday said it favors freeing diesel prices from state control and is finalizing a plan to sell shares in several state-run companies, as New Delhi looks to improve finances strained by populist spending.\par \par \uc2 With the economy stuttering and economists and global ratings companies expressing concerns about India's widening budget deficit, Prime Minister Manmohan Singh's government may now have to take steps to both reduce its expenses such as that on subsidies.\par \par \uc2 "If fuel prices are increased we will see the suppressed inflation out in the market, which may flow into generalized inflation," said the chief dealer at a state-run bank.\par \par \uc2 The RBI is scheduled to sell INR347.15 billion of government bonds, state development loans and treasury bills this week.\par \par \uc2 -By Sourav Mishra, Dow Jones Newswires; +91-22-61456117; nupur.acharya@dowjones.com [ 24-04-12 1244GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120424e84o000yc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
