\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee posts biggest fall in almost a month\b0\par\par\uc2 452 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 2012\par 14:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * USD/INR closes above 52 for 3rd session in row\par \par \uc2 * Traders eye RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; so far none suspected\par \par \uc2 * Near-term outlook for rupee remains weak\par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2 By Aditya Phatak\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, April 23 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee posted its sharpest single session fall in nearly a month on Monday hit by deepening worries over capital inflows, and keeping traders on guard for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The near-term outlook for the rupee remains weak. Concerns over growth and a lack of clarity about further interest rate cuts are being compounded by fears about foreign selling on the back of a controversial set of proposed tax rules.\par \par \uc2 Those fears got fresh fuel after Macquarie's Asia hedge fund exited its short positions in Indian single stock futures because of the uncertainty behind the proposed rules. The news also hit domestic equity markets.\par \par \uc2 On top of the domestic concerns, a weak global risk-off day kept the rupee under pressure on Monday.\par \par \uc2 "Demand for dollars is big. Let's see who comes first. A move above 53 or the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2 ," said a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with a private-sector bank.\par \par \uc2 The rupee ended at 52.52 to the dollar, down sharply f rom Friday's close of 52.07/08, and making this the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's biggest one-day fall since March 29, according to Thomson Reuters data.\par \par \uc2 That marked the third session in a row that USD/INR has closed above 52, intensifying talk about whether the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though so far no action is suspected.\par \par \uc2 Many traders in fact expect a retest of the record-low of 54.30 hit mid-December 2011 if the selling pressure on the rupee does not abate.\par \par \uc2 "Writing on the wall is pretty clear. Outlook on rupee is bearish. Foreign inflows are likely to be really subdued given the tax issues, and unlikely to bridge the gap created by the huge pent-up demand for dollars from oil importers and gold," said Subramaniam Sharma, director of brokerage Greenback \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Technical charts suggest resistance for USD/INR at around 52.95-53.00, which is the 76.4 percent retracement of the December-February fall.\par \par \uc2 The one-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts\par \par \uc2 were at 52.08.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most-traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange and the MCX-SX ended at 52.60, while in the United Stock Exchange, it ended at 52.61.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Rafael Nam)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA/RUPEE (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | SNI | SNS | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120426e84n0014s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
