\par\par \b \uc2 Indian Rupee Falls To 15-Week Low; Government Bonds Down\b0\par\par\uc2 408 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 2012\par 14:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par                          At 1200 GMT \par                          Latest      Change \par    USD/INR                52.50      +0.43 \par    8.79% 2021 Bond        8.57%      +3BPs \par    Call Rate              8.31%      +2BPs \par    Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par    Mar                    3.020      -0.065 \par    *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount are midpoints of bid-offer spreads \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee fell to a 15-week low against the U.S. dollar Monday as importers bought the greenback for month-end settlements.\f28 \par \par \uc2 A weak euro and a decline in local stocks also weighed on the rupee.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was at INR52.50 late Monday, down from INR52.07 late Friday. The dollar rose to INR52.57 earlier in the session, a level last seen Jan. 9.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bombay Stock Exchange\uc2 's Sensitive Index fell 1.6% to end at 17,096.68.\par \par \uc2 The euro fell against the dollar Monday in Asia, following French President Nicolas Sarkozy's poor showing in Sunday's first round of presidential vote.\par \par \uc2 Chin Loo Thio, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 , said the absence of strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the dollar's recent climb against the rupee may have sparked panic-buying of the greenback.\par \par \uc2 She said that India's weak domestic fundamentals rather than global cues were to blame for the rupee's fall as peer \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  haven't fared as badly.\par \par \uc2 "If the rupee continues to weaken at this pace, we may see the RBI tighten trading curbs again," she said, tipping the local unit's next major target at 53.50.\par \par \uc2 In December, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had reduced banks' net open position limits and barred firms from cancelling and rebooking forwards contracts. It later eased restrictions on net open position limits on a case-by-case basis.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Indian government bonds fell Monday on concerns of another wave of inflationary pressures, after a weather group said monsoon rainfall may be below normal in parts of the country.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark 8.79% 2021 bond ended at INR101.42, down from Friday's INR101.58.\par \par \uc2 South Asia's annual monsoon rainfall is likely to be normal this year but some parts of southern and northwestern India--an important grain-producing region--may receive below-normal levels of rain, the weather group said Friday.\par \par \uc2 -By Sourav Mishra, Dow Jones Newswires; +91-22-61456117; nupur.acharya@dowjones.com [ 23-04-12 1235GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120423e84n000vy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
