\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee off lows on dlr flows; outlook weak\b0\par\par\uc2 424 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2012\par 04:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Dollar inflows into some local companies aid rupee\par \par \uc2 * Bleak outlook on sagging growth, global economic woes\par \par \uc2 * Suspected dollar sales may have helped rupee - traders\par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2 By Aditya Phatak\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, April 11 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee pulled back from three-month lows on Wednesday aided by dollar inflows into some companies, but subdued risk appetite on global growth worries limited the recovery.\par \par \uc2 The pull back in rupee sparked market talk about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially as a large state-owned bank was believed to have sold dollars persistently around 51.50 levels, but Reuters could not independently verify this.\par \par \uc2 The RBI releases data on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a lag of nearly two months and the latest one on Monday showed that the bank had bought $1.1 billion and sold $1.4 billion in the spot market in February.\par \par \uc2 The RBI, which has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  intermittently to shore up the rupee in the past few months, is suspected to have sold dollars on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The rupee ended at 51.42/43 to the dollar, after hitting a low of 51.64, a level not seen since Jan. 16. It closed at 51.475/485 on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "All things are against the rupee - globally and domestically," said A. Ajith Kumar, senior manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Federal Bank.\par \par \uc2 Weak growth impulses across the globe and a widening current account deficit are also piling pressure on the rupee, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Spanish and Italian debt eased back from a sharp sell-off on Wednesday and shares staged a modest recovery but investors are wary of signs that the euro zone's debt problems are getting worse or that global growth is flagging.\par \par \uc2 India's main share index ended down 0.26 percent in choppy trade.\par \par \uc2 Given the economic challenges, trader focus is on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy announcement next Tuesday for direction.\par \par \uc2 A majority of analysts polled by Reuters are expecting the RBI to cut rates for the first time in three years to help lift sagging growth.\par \par \uc2 The one-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts\par \par \uc2 were at 51.41.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most-traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and on the United Stock Exchange all ended around 51.65, on a total volume of $4.5 billion.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Malini Menon)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA/RUPEE (UPDATE 2) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | SNI | SNS | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120414e84b00011\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
