\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee eases on global growth worries\b0\par\par\uc2 396 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2012\par 04:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Bunched up dollar inflows post long weekend may support\par \par \uc2 * Bleak US jobs data spurs risk aversion, weighs on rupee\par \par \uc2 * Domestic equities fall about 1.2 percent\par \par \uc2 * Rupee seen in 51.20-51.50/dlr range - traders\par \par \uc2 (Updates to mid-morning)\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, April 9 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee eased on Monday after a four-day trading hiatus, as renewed worries over global economic growth due to bleak U.S. jobs data last week hurt appetite for riskier assets like equities.\par \par \uc2 At 10:22 a.m. (0452 GMT), the rupee was at 51.26/27 to the dollar, weaker than its Wednesday's close of 51.055/065. The market was shut on Thursday and Friday for local holidays.\par \par \uc2 "Global sentiment is weak thanks to the U.S. jobs data and equities too are down. So some pressure on the rupee is expected," said a senior foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with a foreign bank.\par \par \uc2 India's main share index was down nearly 1.2 percent, while U.S. payrolls rose far less than expected in March with 120,000 jobs being added last month, the smallest increase since October.\par \par \uc2 However, bunched up dollar inflows, typically seen after market holidays, could provide some support for the rupee, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Traders also expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step in to avert a sharp fall in the rupee. They see the rupee trading between 51.20 and 51.50 to the dollar this week.\par \par \uc2 "Above 51.50, most banks believe the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sell dollars. So anything above that will make market cautious," said a foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with a state-owned bank.\par \par \uc2 The RBI sold a net $7.3 billion in January in the spot market, after sales of $7.8 billion in December. However, the bank has maintained it does not target any particular exchange rate and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  only to smooth volatility.\par \par \uc2 The one-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts\par \par \uc2 were at 51.73.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most-traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and on the United Stock Exchange were all around 51.58, on a total volume of $640 million.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Aditya Phatak; Editing by Aradhana Aravindan)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA/RUPEE (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | M | RBN | SNI | SNS | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120412e8490004h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
