\par\par \b \uc2 RBI chief:mindful of credibility of action for  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 16:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, March 30 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  is mindful of the credibility of its actions, robustness of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and inflation situation while taking a decision on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Governor Duvvuri Subbarao said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Both options--decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  or not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to contain volatility--entail a cost, Subbarao said.\par \par \uc2 "Our effort always is to make an assessment of the forces driving the capital flows and act only to smooth volatility in the exchange rate movement and prevent disruptions to macroeconomic stability," said Subbarao in a speech to business management students in the southern city of Bangalore.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold $19.86 billion from September to January to arrest a sharp fall in the rupee triggered by capital ouflows during the European debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 The Indian unit had touched a all-time low of 54.30 to the dollar on Dec 15 and has been under pressure so far for most of 2012.\par \par \uc2 It suffered its worst fall in four months in March, shedding 3.68 percent, hammered by investor jitters over the impact of high global oil prices on an economy still licking the wounds of a fierce inflation battle that has crimped growth and widened deficits.\par \par \uc2 Subbarao said volatile capital flows also hurt government and corporates who have external debt obligations.\par \par \uc2 "In an outflow situation, financing of the current account deficit could also turn into a problem," Subbarao said.\par \par \uc2 The country's current account deficit, which has been widening steadily since start of fiscal year in April 2011, further rose to 4.3 percent of GDP or $19.6 billion in the December quarter, from 4.1 percent of GDP or $18.4 billion in September quarter as exports slumped and imports rose.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Suvashree Dey Choudhury and Arjun Kashyap; Editing by Subhadip Sircar)\par \par \uc2 INDIA-CBANK/GOVERNOR (URGENT) | SNI | ABN | M | D | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120330e83u0011i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
