\par\par \b \uc2 India  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2 's Subbarao:  \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange \highlight\uc2  Rate Largely Market-Determined\b0\par\par\uc2 233 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 16:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 )--India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate remains largely market determined and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  only to smoothen volatility and prevent macroeconomic instability, Governor Duvvuri Subbarao said Friday.\par \par \uc2 "In doing so [\b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ], we have to be mindful of the inflation situation, the robustness of our \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, and importantly, the credibility of our actions," Subbarao said while addressing students in the southern city of Bangalore.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market during the August-December period to "smoothen the volatility of the exchange rate movement," he added.\par \par \uc2 The rupee fell about 16% against the U.S. dollar in 2011 as the euro-zone jitters magnified concerns over India's twin current account and fiscal deficits, slowing growth and high inflation. It touched a record low of 54.2925 to the U.S. dollar on Dec. 15.\par \par \uc2 Subsequently, the RBI and the government put in place a slew of measures to boost the rupee, such as relaxing foreign investment rules for local debt and equity, freeing interest rates on deposits held by non-resident Indians and easing restrictions on foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrowing for Indian companies.\par \par \uc2 In the January-March quarter, the rupee gained 4.4% against the dollar.\par \pa