\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee down on local shares, risk aversion\b0\par\par\uc2 445 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 04:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Proposed tax changes spark fund outflow fears\par \par \uc2 * Subdued risk appetite on global growth worries adds to gloom\par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, background, updates to mid-morning)\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, March 29 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee weakened on Thursday on lingering concerns proposed tax laws could trigger a sell-off in local equities by foreign funds, with global risk taking already taking a knock from sluggish U.S. and China economic data.\par \par \uc2 "The policy confusion, reform paralysis and growth worries are all hurting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with a foreign bank.\par \par \uc2 The main stock index has lost more than 2 percent this week and foreign brokerages are complaining that recent provisions to tax indirect investments and combat tax evasion are couched in ambiguous language and could also be used to target overseas market investors.\par \par \uc2 Payments by oil importers, the biggest buyers of dollars in the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, are also putting pressure on the rupee, traders said.\par \par \uc2 At 11:16 a.m. (0546 GMT), the rupee was at 51.11/12 to the dollar, weaker than Wednesday's close of 50.7750/7850.\par \par \uc2 It dropped to as much as 51.2250 at one stage before pulling back slightly, sparking speculation of likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  but traders said some foreign banks sold dollars.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-run banks to curb excessive volatility, but it does not comment on such activity until the data is released with a lag of about two months.\par \par \uc2 The outlook for the rupee remains subdued, with the charts suggesting initial support at 51.27, which is a 76.4 percent Fibonacci retracement of this week's range. The next support would be at 51.45, the 50 percent retracement of the rupee's rise between December and February.\par \par \uc2 The one-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts\par \par \uc2 were at 51.55.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most-traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and on the United Stock Exchange were all around 51.47, on a combined volume of $1.37 billion.\par \par \uc2 Shares across Asian markets were subdued on worries over slowing growth in the United States and China.\par \par \uc2 New orders for U.S. durables increased only modestly in February, below analysts' forecasts, while a gauge of future business investment also fell short of expectations, raising the prospect that economic growth in the first quarter could be lacklustre.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Aditya Phatak; Additional reporting by Krishna Kumar; Editing by Ranjit Gangadharan)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA/RUPEE (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | SNI | SNS | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120401e83t00010\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
