\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee drops to lowest in more than 2 months\b0\par\par\uc2 403 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 04:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Oil import payments weigh down rupee\par \par \uc2  * Subdued shares douse capital inflow hopes \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, background, updates to mid-morning)\par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, March 26 (Reuters) - The rupee gave up early gains and skidded to its lowest in more than two months on Monday, pressured by oil payments and subdued shares.\par \par \uc2  India imports about 80 percent of the oil the country consumes and refiners are the biggest buyers of dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, with their demand tending to peak towards the close of each month when they make payments.\par \par \uc2  Tension between Iran and United States is likely keep demand for dollars strong as Indian companies would look to clear import dues as early as possible before any financial sanctions are imposed on Iran's customers, traders said.\par \par \uc2  New Delhi, which buys nearly 12 percent of its oil needs from Tehran, could be exempted from tighter U.S. sanctions,   the International Energy Agency's executive director told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  At 10:54 a.m. (0524 GMT), the rupee was at 51.27/28 to the dollar, weaker than last week's close of 51.17/18. It weakened as far as 51.30, a level last seen on Jan. 16 according to Thomson Reuters data.\par \par \uc2  The drop was halted on expectation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smoothen volatility. The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  is suspected to have sold dollar on two occasions last week to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2  "Outlook on the rupee seems a bit bearish as month-end dollar demand from oil companies will be strong," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with a brokerage. "On top of this equities too look weak." \par \par \uc2  The main share index was down more than 1 percent on worries about growth and stalled reforms encouraged market players to roll over short positions before the expiry of monthly derivatives on Thursday.\par \par \uc2  Technical charts too point towards possibility of more pressure on the rupee. See, \par \par \uc2  The one-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts\par \par \uc2 were at 51.84.\par \par \uc2  In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most-traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and the United Stock Exchange were all around 51.31, on a total volume of $1.29 billion. \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Aditya Phatak; Editing by Ranjit Gangadharan)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA/RUPEE (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | SNI | SNS | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120329e83q0003i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
