 importers and companies with overseas debt ahead of the close of the financial year on March 31 is making \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  difficult.\par \par \uc2 In a research note, Standard Chartered Bank said the RBI may scale down its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near term to preserve \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in case the dollar rises to INR52.00-INR53.00 levels.\par \par \uc2 - By Sourav Mishra and Sudeep Jain, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 6145 6123; sudeep.jain@dowjones.com [ 26-03-12 1143GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120326e83q000pn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
