\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Deputy Gov: May  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  More In  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Markets If See 'Strong One Way Risk' For Rupee\b0\par\par\uc2 By Chester Yung  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 07:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  further in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if it sees a "strong one way risk" for the Indian rupee, Deputy Gov. Subir Gokarn said Friday.\par \par \uc2 "We see the return of some instability in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Gokarn told Dow Jones Newswires in an interview on the sidelines of the Credit Suisse Asian Investor Conference.\par \par \uc2 "We don't target a range (for the rupee), but when there's a risk of moving strongly one way, that's something we want to avoid," he said.\par \par \uc2 Gokarn's comments come as the rupee is trading at an over two-month low to the dollar. The rupee slipped to a record low against the dollar last year following mounting global uncertainty and slowing growth in Asia's third-largest economy, which has been impacted by an extended period of inflation.\par \par \uc2 The senior \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  official said the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was relatively stable between January and February. In the last few days, however, he said there has been some instability in the rupee.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, RBI Adviser Ashima Goyal said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to ensure that the rupee doesn't weaken significantly beyond its fair value of INR50 to the dollar.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations affect software companies to a large extent as they book most of their revenue in dollars, but settle the majority of their costs in rupees.\par \par \uc2 On the inflation front, Gokarn said he has seen some moderation in inflation, while domestic demand remains strong. However, he warned that the recent sharp rise in oil prices will pose new risks to price pressures.\par \par \uc2 Earlier Friday, Gokarn said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is moving toward looser monetary policy, though the timing for easing will depend on the state of the economy.\par \par \uc2 At its rate-setting meeting on March 15, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left its key lending rate unchanged, saying risks to inflation have increased due to a recent spurt in crude oil prices, a wide fiscal deficit and a weakening rupee.\par \par \uc2 -By Chester Yung, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2832 2331; chester.yung@dowjones.com [ 03-23-12 0309ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020120323e83n0000r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
