\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2 's adviser favours no  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market now\b0\par\par\uc2 188 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 13:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 NEW DELHI, March 23 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  need not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as of now to prop up a weakening rupee, the chief economic adviser in the finance ministry said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee ended at 51.17/18 to the dollar on Thursday, after touching the day's low of 51.28, a level not seen since Jan. 16. The unit had closed at 50.66/67 on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "This is not that place where I would recommend \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Kaushik Basu said.\par \par \uc2 The Indian rupee pared some of the losses on Thursday on suspected dollar sales by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "I have, for a long time, felt that rupee being at a level it is, is not unnatural at all, given the fact that India has had greater inflation than the U.S.," Basu said.\par \par \uc2 Indian money markets were closed on Friday for a public holiday.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Arup Roychoudhury; editing by Malini Menon; )\par \par \uc2 INDIA-ECONOMY/ADVISER (URGENT) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | SNI | SNS | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120323e83n000nz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
