\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee off 2-mo low on possible RBI dlr sales\b0\par\par\uc2 559 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 03:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * RBI suspected to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  near 51.25-51.28/dlr\par \par \uc2 * Weak PMI data from China, Europe hurts risk hunger\par \par \uc2 * Local shares slide over 2 percent\par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, comments, updates to close)\par \par \uc2 By Aditya Phatak\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, March 22 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee dropped to its weakest in more than two months on Thursday after weak Chinese and euro zone manufacturing data hit demand for risk, but suspected dollar sales by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  pulled the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back from the day's lows.\par \par \uc2 Fears foreign investors would turn net sellers of Indian stocks also contributed to the rupee's fall after the prime minister's office moved to quell an outcry over a reported $211 billion loss in revenues from the sale of coalfields.\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee ended at 51.17/18 to the dollar, after sliding to as low as 51.28 earlier, a level not seen since Jan. 16. The unit had closed at 50.66/67 on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a second in a session in a row to shore up the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has dropped around 2 percent in nearly a week.\par \par \uc2 "Global factors weighed more than domestic reasons, as unexpected weakness in euro zone PMI data caused a massive risk sell-off and hit \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the board," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for a foreign bank in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 The sell-off in the rupee accelerated after Germany and France reported an unexpected contraction in manufacturing activity, adding to earlier data showing China's economy is also slowing down.\par \par \uc2 Traders are closely looking at how foreign investors will react to a government under pressure. The coalfield sale report came on a day when India also announced a sweeping rollback of a rail fare hike.\par \par \uc2 That is adding to broad disappointment after India last week announced a bigger-than-expected borrowing plan as part of its 2012/13 budget.\par \par \uc2 "Post the budget, signs of optimism on India have reduced and could put the foreign institutional investors on a wait-and-watch mode," said J. Moses Harding, head of the asset liability committee at \uc2 IndusInd Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Persistent and large dollar demand from local oil importers as well as caution before the extended weekend hurt rupee, traders said. Debt and money markets will be closed on Friday for a public holiday, though stock exchanges will be open.\par \par \uc2 "Dollar demand is coming in thick and fast because tensions between Iran and United States are just going up," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with a state-owned bank. "So importers will want to get their payments settled as soon as possible."\par \par \uc2 India imports more than 80 percent of its oil requirements, including a significant chunk from Iran, and the country's oil refiners are major buyers of dollars in the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market..\par \par \uc2 The one-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts\par \par \uc2 were at 51.69.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most-traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and the United Stock Exchange all ended around 51.30, on a total volume of $6.69 billion.\par \par \uc2 