\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee wipes gains as local shares fall\b0\par\par\uc2 485 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 03:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Turnover in rupee/dlr trade seen subdued\par \par \uc2 * Domestic equities fall more than 1 percent\par \par \uc2 * Rupee may face selling pressure before fiscal year end-traders\par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, comments, updates to close)\par \par \uc2 By Aditya Phatak\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, March 19 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee fell back on Monday as local stocks dropped for the third straight session and foreign capital inflows dried up during the session amid subdued volumes towards the close of the fiscal year.\par \par \uc2 The rupee is seen moving in a range of 49.85 to 50.50 to the dollar this week, although some traders did not rule out a bout of selling towards the end of the month as banks close accounts for the 2011/12 fiscal year.\par \par \uc2 The rupee ended at 50.23/24 to the dollar, after rising to 50.0650 in early trades. It had closed at 50.175/185 on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Dollar inflows into local debt likely supported the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  early in the session. However, a fall in local equities pulled the rupee lower.\par \par \uc2 The inflows had came after an auction on Friday of unused limits, which allow foreign institutional investors to buy long-term government and corporate bonds, was oversubscribed.\par \par \uc2 "49.85 has emerged as a very strong resistance for the rupee and as the year end approaches traders will look to crystallise profits," said Naveen Raghuvanshi, associate vice president of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at \uc2 Development Credit Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It is also the quarter end and the month end, so market could turn biddish (on the dollar)."\par \par \uc2 The government's budget for 2012/13 was also seen as negative for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since it offered no new solutions to address the country's fiscal constraints, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Rating agency Moody's Investors Service said the budget was credit negative for Asia's third largest economy.\par \par \uc2 Technical charts also hinted at selling pressure on the rupee if it failed to strengthen past the 50 level soon, b ut most traders expect any sharp slide in the rupee to be cut short by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been actively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market over the past few months to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in case of acute selling pressure.\par \par \uc2 The RBI sold a net $7.3 billion in January in the spot market, after sales of $7.8 billion in December, data released by the RBI last week showed.\par \par \uc2 The one-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts\par \par \uc2 were at 50.71.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most-traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange ended at 50.3625, on the MCX-SX at 50.3700 and on the United Stock Exchange at 50.3400, on a total volume of $3.29 billion.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Aradhana Aravindan)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA/RUPEE (UPDATE 1) | ABN | M | RBN | SNI | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120322e83j0003s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
