\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: India  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Likely To Have Sold Dollars To Protect Rupee\b0\par\par\uc2 557 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 13:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely began when dollar was at INR50.52, dealers say\par \par \uc2 --RBI likely to stop dollar from appreciating above INR51.00, analyst says\par \par \uc2 --Wednesday's suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least the second this week\par \par \uc2 (Recasts 1st paragraph, updates \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  level in 4th paragraph, analyst's quote in 7th paragraph and background in 8th-13th paragraphs)\par \par \uc2 By Sourav Mishra and Sudeep Jain\par \par \uc2 OF DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 )--\b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for at least the second time this week Wednesday to prop up the rupee after the local unit fell to a seven-week low against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  likely started selling dollars when the greenback was trading around INR50.52, five dealers told Dow Jones Newswires.\par \par \uc2 The suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped push the rupee into positive territory after it slumped to a seven-week low of 50.76 to a dollar, according to the dealers who spoke on the customary condition of anonymity.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was quoted at INR50.28 in late Asian trade Wednesday, down from 50.36 Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The RBI's suspected presence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets comes as the rupee has lost about 3% against the greenback over the past five sessions. Rising concerns over Greece's ability to avoid a sovereign default and jitters about slowing global economic growth have triggered a selloff in riskier assets, including equities and a wide array of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the rupee and Korean won and the Australian dollar.\par \par \uc2 Analysts expect the RBI to ramp up its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the rupee continues to weaken.\par \par \uc2 "The Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not allow rupee weakness beyond the 51.00 mark and may support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it approaches this level," said Moses Harding, head of global markets at \uc2 IndusInd Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The volatility in local debt, equity and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets is likely to increase in the run-up to the RBI's rate-setting meeting on Mar. 15, which will be followed a day later by the federal government's budget announcement for the fiscal year starting April 1.\par \par \uc2 Wednesday's suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  follows a similar move on Monday, when the RBI is believed to have started selling dollars when the greenback was trading around INR49.90.\par \par \uc2 The RBI didn't comment on the suspected actions, but it's public position is that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  only to dampen exchange-rate volatility and not to protect a particular \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  level. It discloses data on its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions with a lag of more than a month.\par \par \uc2 Data disclosed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  show the RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to protect the local unit as it fell to a record low of 54.2925 to a dollar in mid-December.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $7.8 billion of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in December--its highest monthly sale since the peak of the financial crisis in October 2008.\par \par \uc2 The rupee's recent losses follow gains of much as 9% against the dollar earlier this year on a surge in portfolio capital inflows following measures to ease foreign investment restrictions in capital markets.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By Sourav Mishra & Sudeep Jain; Dow Jones Newswires; 91-22-61456112 sourav.mishra@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 07-03-12 1201GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120307e837000py\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
