\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee hits 1-month low on importer demand\b0\par\par\uc2 401 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 03:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Rupee hits 49.8175/dlr, weakest since Jan. 27\par \par \uc2  * Market on lookout for possible dlr sales by RBI to support rupee \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, background, updates to mid-morning)\par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, March 5 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee dropped to its weakest level in more than a month on Monday due to dollar demand from importers and a fall in local shares, prompting traders to lookout for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall.\par \par \uc2  At 10:44 a.m. (0514 GMT), the rupee was at 49.74/75 to the dollar, after dipping to 49.8175, a level last seen on Jan. 27, according to Thomson Reuters data. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had closed at 49.50/51 on Friday.\par \par \uc2  "Traders are wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; so despite the current selling pressure on the rupee, the fall may be gradual," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer with a state-run bank.\par \par \uc2  Many dealers expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to supply dollars if the rupee closes in on the 50 level.\par \par \uc2  The RBI has actively participated in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market over the last few months, selling dollars while simultaneously resorting to a flurry of steps aimed at cutting speculation and improving dollar inflows.\par \par \uc2  Data released by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month showed it sold more than $9 billion in the spot and forwards markets in December, its biggest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in nearly three-and-half years. \par \par \uc2  The rupee, which had erased around 16 percent of its value against the dollar in 2011, has rebounded by over 6.5 percent so far this year, primarily due to the strong foreign investor appetite for Indian shares and debt, where they have invested more than $12.5 billion.\par \par \uc2  Nonetheless, the tepid response to the government's $2.5 billion stake sale in ONGC last week has raised doubts abut the continuation of the dollar inflows, traders said.\par \par \uc2  One-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts \par \par \uc2  were at 50.21.\par \par \uc2  In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most-traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and the United Stock Exchange were all around 50.02, on a total volume of $1.07 billion. \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Aditya Phatak; Editing by Rajesh Pandathil)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA/RUPEE (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | SNI | SNS | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120308e83500047\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
