\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: India  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Says Has Room To Cut Cash Reserve Ratio Further\b0\par\par\uc2 517 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 11:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    --Open to using all instruments to manage liquidity, official says \par    --Inflation risks emerging with rising oil prices \par    --Growth not sole driver of monetary policy, official says \par    --Reducing statutory liquidity ratio won't ease liquidity crunch \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Adds comments in 6th-8th, 10th and 12th paragraphs, background in 3rd-5th paragraphs)\f28 \par \par \uc2 By Sourav Mishra and Sudeep Jain\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 )--India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has room to reduce banks' minimum cash requirement further, a top official said Monday, adding that it is open to using all instruments to manage liquidity.\par \par \uc2 "If we think its appropriate to use it [a cash reserve ratio cut] we will, and it is certainly on the table," Reserve Bank of India Deputy Governor Subir Gokarn said on television in comments indicating that a CRR cut may come at the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2 's next policy meeting on March 15.\par \par \uc2 The comments come against the backdrop of an acute liquidity shortage, which hasn't eased despite frequent bond buybacks and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move on Jan. 24 to cut the CRR by half a percentage point to 5.50%.\par \par \uc2 The cash reserve ratio is the minimum percentage of deposits that banks must hold with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The cash shortage--brought on by fiscal third-quarter advance tax payments in December and the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to prop up the Indian rupee--is expected to worsen when companies pay advance taxes for the January-March quarter in the middle of March.\par \par \uc2 A cut in the statutory liquidity ratio--banks' mandatory bond holding requirement--would not be effective as most banks hold bonds in excess of the minimum requirement, Gokarn told reporters separately.\par \par \uc2 He told the CNBC TV-18 television channel that growth considerations weren't the sole driver of monetary policy, and that some risks to inflation are emerging, such as the recent rise in crude oil prices.\par \par \uc2 India's gross domestic product growth slowed to a more than two-year low of 6.1% in the October-December quarter, hurt by successive interest rate increases and a weak external environment.\par \par \uc2 The timing and magnitude of rate cuts would be conditioned by the emerging risks, Gokarn added.\par \par \uc2 The RBI left its policy rate unchanged at its previous two rate-setting meetings after a staggering 13 increases over the past two years.\par \par \uc2 Gokarn also said the government's fiscal stance needs to be consistent with the RBI's monetary stance and he expects the government to take some steps in this direction when it presents its next budget on March 16.\par \par \uc2 In its previous policy statement, the RBI said it would be constrained from lowering rates in the absence of credible fiscal consolidation.\par \par \uc2 India is expected to widely overshoot its aim of keeping the fiscal deficit within 4.6% of its gross domestic product in the current fiscal year through March.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   --By Sudeep Jain, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 6145 6123; sudeep.jain@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 05-03-12 1033GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120305e835000p2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
