\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-UPDATE 1-RBI's Dec  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  market  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  biggest in 3-1/2 years\b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 2012\par 03:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Repeats story issued late on Monday)\par \par \uc2 * RBI sold $9.18 bln in Dec; highest since Oct 2008\par \par \uc2 * Rupee hit record low of 54.30/dlr on Dec. 15\par \par \uc2 * Recent rebound in rupee may be shortlived-traders\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Feb 13 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India (RBI) \uc2 sold more than $9 billion in the spot and forwards market in December 2011, its biggest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in nearly three-and-half years to prop up the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from its record low of 54.30.\par \par \uc2 Traders expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rupee as they believe its rebound this year could be cut short as the economy struggles with twin deficits and high inflation.\par \par \uc2 The RBI's victory in reversing a sharp decline in the rupee may be short-lived and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will remain vulnerable unless the problems of hefty fiscal and current account deficits are addressed. For an analysis, see:\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a net $7.81 billion in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in December, up from $2.92 billion in the previous month, the bank said in its bulletin for February.\par \par \uc2 The RBI net sold $1.37 billion in the forwards market in December, lower than $1.62 billion in the previous month, taking the total dollar sales in December to $9.18 billion, its biggest \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since October 2008.\par \par \uc2 The rupee has rebounded nearly 8 percent since January after plunging nearly 16 percent in 2011 when it was the worst performing major Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "They are unlikely to allow the rupee to cross the 50 per dollar mark very easily," said a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a foreign bank, referring to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It would prefer selling a billion dollars now rather than 4 to 5 billion dollars at higher levels."\par \par \uc2 The rupee ended at 49.19/20 to the dollar on Monday, stronger than its Friday's close of 49.40/41.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Suvashree Dey Choudhury and Aditya Phatak; editing by Malini Menon)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -RBI-\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1) (REPEAT)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120214e82e0003g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
