\par\par \b \uc2 REFILE-POLL-Indian rupee to hold steady in 2012, portfolio flows key\b0\par\par\uc2 750 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 2012\par 08:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Refiles to remove extraneous matter)\par \par \uc2 * For results click on\par \par \uc2 * Rupee to fluctuate between 50.0 and 48.8 in 2012, end year flat\par \par \uc2 * Stimulus abroad, India's ability to attract portfolio flows key to rupee\par \par \uc2 By Rahul Karunakar\par \par \uc2 BANGALORE, Feb 3 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee is expected to hold steady through much of this year, encumbered by an economy that will struggle to attract the portfolio flows it needs to fund to its balance of payments, a Reuters poll showed.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not revisit the record lows it hit in mid-December, the poll showed.\par \par \uc2 But the rapid slowdown in the economy and persistently high inflation make India a relatively less attractive investment destination, even in a year when developed economies are expected to pump massive stimulus into financial markets.\par \par \uc2 The Reuters poll of 28 strategists and analysts, taken this week, saw the rupee trading at 50.0 against the dollar in a month, 50.5 in three months and strengthening to 48.8 a year from now, which is close to Friday's spot market levels of 49.03. That compared with 52.0, 51.4 and 49.0 in the December poll.\par \par \uc2 Expectations are already running high for another round of bond purchases from the U.S. Federal Reserve and for the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lend more to its troubled banking system. Analysts expect a lot of that cash will flow towards emerging markets and commodities.\par \par \uc2 Yet, further strength in the rupee may depend on investor confidence in prospects for a global recovery as well as a snapback in India's domestic economy.\par \par \uc2 "If we see global risk appetite improve from here then dollar/rupee could fall further," said Nick Verdi, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 "But we think weak fundamentals will limit rupee appreciation from here," he said, making a specific reference to India's weak fiscal position .\par \par \uc2 After losing 16 percent of its value last year, the rupee recouped about half of those losses on \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a general rush back into riskier assets among global investors.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors put about $2 billion into Indian markets in January alone, after being net sellers in 2011. The rupee posted its largest monthly gain in over 17 years in January, rising 7.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 Yet a current account deficit as wide as 3 percent of economic output plus weak foreign direct investment and a pipeline of maturing foreign borrowings make it imperative that India keeps attracting foreign money into its stock and bond markets.\par \par \uc2 Economists in a separate Reuters poll cut their forecasts for India's economy and now expect it to grow 7.6 percent in the fiscal year to March, its slowest pace in two years. The economy grew 6.9 percent in the quarter ended September 2011.\par \par \uc2 After 13 rate rises to stamp out inflation in between March 2010 and October 2011, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  signalled last month it was shifting its focus to growth by cutting the cash reserve requirements for banks by 50 basis points.\par \par \uc2 "The fact that inflation is more sticky in India than in most other economies in the rest of the region is limiting the extent to which the RBI can loosen monetary policy," said Verdi.\par \par \uc2 The RBI also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  many times in the market late last year, selling dollars in an attempt to prop up the rupee, which fell to a record low of 54.30 against the dollar on Dec. 15.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also announced a series of measures aimed at cutting out speculative bets on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and boosting capital inflows into Asia's third largest economy. .\par \par \uc2 That \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  stabilised the rupee, and possibly transferred some of the bearish bets into the offshore rupee markets. One-year offshore non-deliverable forward contracts\par \par \uc2 were at 51.85 earlier on Friday, effectively pricing in a 5 percent depreciation in the next 12 months.\par \par \uc2 Analysts also noted that, like any \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the impact of the RBI measures are not long-lasting.\par \par \uc2 "Most of these measures are temporary in nature and while they are good for the near term stability of the rupee they are negative for long term sustainability," said Bhupesh Bameta at Quant Capital.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Ross Finley and Vidya Ranganathan; Polling by Ashrith Doddi and Namrata Anchan in Bangalore and Anooja Debnath in Singapore)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/POLL (EMBARGO 0615 GMT) (CORRE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120206e823000hc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
