\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: India  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Says  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Trading Curbs Temporary\b0\par\par\uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 2012\par 09:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Will reverse curbs when they are no longer necessary, deputy governor says\par \par \uc2 --No room for aggressive rate cuts as commodity prices remain high\par \par \uc2 --Liquidity deficit remains above \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comfort zone\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to consider bond buybacks\par \par \uc2 (Recasts the first paragraph, adds deputy governor's comments in 4th, 8th and 10th paragraphs, analyst's comment in 7th paragraph, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  level in 6th paragraph)\par \par \uc2 By Sourav Mishra and Sudeep Jain\par \par \uc2 Of \uc2 DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 )--The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  could reverse its recent curbs on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading once markets stabilize as they run counter to its capital account management strategy, a top official said Friday, indicating that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now more comfortable with the rupee's trading range.\par \par \uc2 There will be a situation when the restrictions will no longer be necessary and "we will take the situation back to where it was," RBI Deputy Governor Subir Gokarn told reporters after a conference, without disclosing any specific timeline for reversing the measures.\par \par \uc2 In December, the RBI placed limits on unhedged foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions that banks can hold overnight and also banned companies from cancelling and rebooking forward contracts with the same underlying exposure as part of measures to prop up the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The whole purpose of our capital management strategy is to bring as much liquidity into the market as possible, as many legitimate participants as possible, and when we impose curbs, we are actually restricting the space," Gokarn said.\par \par \uc2 The RBI had imposed the curbs after the rupee slumped to a record low of 54.2925 to a U.S. dollar on Dec. 15. The local unit, which dropped 16% versus the greenback in 2011, has jumped more than 11% from its record low and is up about 9% in 2012, thanks to the RBI's curbs and direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well as improving global risk appetite and \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's measures to boost capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 Friday, the dollar was at INR48.88 at 0808 GMT.\par \par \uc2 Partha Mukherjee, president of treasury and international banking at \uc2 Axis Bank\uc2 , said that, even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might not reverse those curbs immediately, Gokarn's comments are positive for the markets as they indicate that the RBI is increasingly at ease with the rupee's level.\par \par \uc2 Separately, Gokarn told the CNBC-TV18 television channel that, unlike in 2008, the RBI doesn't currently have room for aggressive rate cuts as commodity prices remain high.\par \par \uc2 Slowing economic growth and easing inflation have fuelled hopes that monetary easing is imminent. The RBI had raised rates a staggering 13 times over the past two years, but left rates unchanged at its last two rate-setting meetings.\par \par \uc2 Gokarn also said the liquidity deficit in the banking system remains above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comfort zone of INR600 billion, and the RBI would continue to consider open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as bond buybacks to ease the cash crunch.\par \par \uc2 - By Sourav Mishra and Sudeep Jain, \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\uc2 ; 91 22 6145 6123; sudeep.jain@dowjones.com [ 03-02-12 0813GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120203e823000pk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
