\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE: India Official: Rupee's Rise Not A Sign Of Economic Bounceback\b0\par\par\uc2 717 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 2012\par 10:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   --Indian rupee's gain due to capital inflows, steps by authorities, says official \par   --\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strongly in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market at current levels, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par  \par   (Recasts 1st paragraph, updates \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  level in 4th paragraph, adds analysts' comments in 6th and 18th paragraph) \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By Abhrajit Gangopadhyay and Sudeep Jain\f28 \par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 NEW DELHI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee's recent surge isn't really a sign of--or even backed by--a strong economic recovery, a top government official cautioned Friday, giving weight to comments from analysts who have warned over the past few weeks that they see little evidence the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  can sustain its rise.\par \par \uc2 "The Indian rupee is appreciating due to foreign capital inflows, and previous steps taken by the authorities are also helping," the Finance Ministry official, who asked not to be named, told Dow Jones Newswires.\par \par \uc2 The comments, from one of the country's most senior officials, come at a time when the rupee is at an 11-week high against the U.S. dollar, and traders appear to be bullish on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar was trading at INR49.39 at 0921 GMT--its lowest level since Nov. 9, 2011. The greenback has lost nearly 9% from the record high of INR54.2925 reached on Dec. 15, 2011.\par \par \uc2 Despite this, the Finance Ministry official's views are backed by analysts, who believe that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise shouldn't be taken to signal a revival of the Indian economy, and that traders should look through the euphoria and study the basics instead.\par \par \uc2 Investment bank \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  said in a recent research note that it doesn't think that the "underlying fundamentals have shifted that much in 2012, so we remain skeptical that the INR [rupee] outperformance can continue."\par \par \uc2 Watchers attribute the rupee's recent rise to a range of measure taken by the government and the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  coupled with improved global risk appetite, and outright \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors have already put a net $4.8 billion into local debt and stocks in 2012 so far--compared with $8.3 billion in the whole of 2011--following measures to ease foreign investment restrictions in capital markets.\par \par \uc2 Also, the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has actively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to prop up the rupee, with its dollar sales rising to a 32-month high of $2.9 billion in November.\par \par \uc2 Last month, the RBI placed limits on the unhedged \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions that banks can hold overnight, and banned companies from cancelling and rebooking forwards contracts to clamp down on what it called speculative behavior.\par \par \uc2 RBI Governor Duvvuri Subbarao Tuesday said the restrictions may not be temporary.\par \par \uc2 That aside, there is much to be concerned about.\par \par \uc2 India runs a persistent current account deficit due to a large trade gap, which is likely to increase given the weak global outlook for exports and the non-discretionary nature of India's major imports such as crude oil.\par \par \uc2 India's July-September current account gap widened to $16.9 billion from $15.8 billion in the April-June quarter.\par \par \uc2 Another concern is India's fiscal deficit, which is expected to overshoot the government's target of 4.6% of gross domestic product for the current fiscal year through March by as much as 1 percentage point.\par \par \uc2 While government spending has remained high in the run-up to state elections in five states this year, tax revenue has taken a hit due to a slowing economy.\par \par \uc2 In the July-September quarter, India's gross domestic product grew 6.9%--the lowest reading in more than two years.\par \par \uc2 Investors are now watching how the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will respond to the rupee's recent rise. It may not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  strongly at current levels, said Chin Loo Thio, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bank has a stated policy of not revealing if it has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  or not, and it says that it will step in only to curb volatility. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   --By Abhrajit Gangopadhyay and Sudeep Jain, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 6145 6123; sudeep.jain@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 27, 2012 04:25 ET (09:25 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120127e81r002o9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
