\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee up for 4th week; dollar inflows aid\b0\par\par\uc2 497 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 2012\par 03:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Local shares end up 0.9 pct, helps rupee\par \par \uc2 * Next immediate support for dollar seen at 49.20 level - trader\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, quotes, updates to close)\par \par \uc2 By Shamik Paul\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Jan 27 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee gained for the fourth straight week aided by positive local shares and robust dollar inflows, while the outlook remained bullish for the local unit.\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee ended at 49.3050/3150 to the dollar, after touching 49.2975, its highest since Nov. 8, and firmer than 50.09/10 at close on Wednesday. The market was closed on Thursday for a local holiday.\par \par \uc2 "All the factors are looking positive for the rupee, in addition to RBI's strictures on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said J. Moses Harding, head of the asset-liabilities committee at \uc2 IndusInd Bank\uc2 . "The supply has been tremendous from foreign funds."\par \par \uc2 "49.20 is the next immediate support for the dollar. If we break that, we will be staring at a low on 48.51," he said.\par \par \uc2 RBI Governor Duvvuri Subbarao said on Tuesday that the curbs that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has put in place to prevent speculation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market may not be temporary in nature.\par \par \uc2 Indian shares rose for a sixth straight session to a 11-week high as foreign investors continued to buy local stocks on indication of a policy shift towards reviving growth, with an increase in global risk appetite also aiding sentiment.\par \par \uc2 Foreign institutional investors have bought Indian shares worth $1.8 billion so far in January, and invested $3.4 billion in debt.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, in addition to the spot market, to help manage liquidity in the banking system, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  source said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 For more stories on recent measures taken to shore up the rupee, see\par \par \uc2 Traders said a weak dollar overseas also aided the rupee.\par \par \uc2 The yen was on track to post its biggest daily gain in a month against the dollar, recouping most losses made earlier this week as hedge funds bought the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the euro consolidated awaiting a breakthrough in Greek debt talks.\par \par \uc2 The market developments in Greece would provide directional cues and influence dollar inflows into India, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The European Union and IMF want Greece to push through more budget cuts and implement a series of long-agreed austerity reforms before they agree on a new bailout the country needs to avert bankruptcy, a report obtained by Reuters showed.\par \par \uc2 One-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts were at 49.68, indicating some weakness in the short term in the onshore spot rate.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most-traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and the United Stock Exchange all ended around 49.6 on total volumes of $4.8 billion.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Subhadip Sircar)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA/RUPEE (UPDATE 3)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120130e81r0003f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
