\par\par \b \uc2 2nd UPDATE: Indian Rupee Rises To Near 6-Week High On Capital Inflows\b0\par\par\uc2 594 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 2012\par 14:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Indian rupee near six-week high as foreign cash flows into local debt\par \par \uc2 -- Foreign funds in local debt so far in 2012 totals INR101.13 billion, up from INR17.09 billion year ago\par \par \uc2 -- Rupee's rise comes day after traders said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars heavily\par \par \uc2 -- India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell to over 12-month low in first week of January, indicating RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in 3rd-4th paragraph, updates \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  level in 5th paragraph.)\par \par \uc2 By Sourav Mishra\par \par \uc2 Of \uc2 DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 )--The Indian rupee rose to a near six-week high against the U.S. dollar Friday, driven by capital flows into local debt as a series of measures to attract foreign cash began to pay off.\par \par \uc2 The rise--which helped to further reverse some of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's large selloff last year--came after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was Thursday spotted selling dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is whittling down \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which fell to a more than 12-month low of $293.54 billion in the first week of January, data showed Friday.\par \par \uc2 The reserves were at record high of $320.80 billion in September.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was at INR51.53 late Friday in Asia, after falling to an intraday low of INR51.29, its weakest level since Dec. 5 and down from INR51.60 Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Despite the rupee's recent rise, market analysts warned that the rally is unlikely to continue unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  clearly shows that it has shifted its focus to helping growth rather than fighting inflation.\par \par \uc2 They added that, if the Reserve Bank cuts rates at its Jan. 24 policy meeting, it would signal to foreign investors that it is supporting the economy, and that would in turn lead to increased capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 Apart from continuing concerns over a ballooning fiscal deficit and a gaping current account gap which could widen due to India's unfavorable trade balance, steady demand for the greenback to settle bills for oil imports and defense purchases also clouds the rupee's long-term prospects.\par \par \uc2 Philip Wee, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at \uc2 DBS Group Holdings\uc2 , said investors may wait to see what the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says on Jan. 24 before pouring in more foreign capital.\par \par \uc2 The rupee was Asia's worst-performing major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2011, with the dollar gaining about 19% against the rupee. The greenback has lost about 3.3% against the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far in 2012.\par \par \uc2 India recently raised foreign investment limits in government and corporate bonds by $5 billion each to $15 billion and $20 billion, respectively. The time for investing in these government bonds ends Friday.\par \par \uc2 It also relaxed regulations for overseas investments in shares, and allowed banks to freely set interest rates on deposits from non-resident Indians.\par \par \uc2 The steps were aimed at attracting foreign capital, which had dried out in the past year due to slowing growth and diminishing risk appetite.\par \par \uc2 Also, an upgrade of India's ratings by \uc2 Moody's\uc2  late December improved appetite for government debt, which offers yields much higher than other major economies.\par \par \uc2 The effects of the measures were evident in data from the capital markets regulator, which show foreign funds have invested INR101.13 billion in Indian debt so far in 2012, compared with INR17.09 billion a year earlier.\par \par \uc2 -By Sourav Mishra, \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\uc2 ; 91-22-61456112 sourav.mishra@dowjones.com [ 13-01-12 1333GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120113e81d000tr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
