\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE: India  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2 's Heavy Dollar Sales In November Point To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 545 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2012\par 11:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   --\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold $2.9 billion in November, highest since March 2009 \par   --Rupee fell 7% against U.S. dollar in November \par   --Analyst says \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  likely remained heavy in December \par  \par   (Recasts 1st paragraph, adds analyst's comment in 2nd paragraph, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  level in 6th paragraph and additional details throughout) \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By Sudeep Jain\f28 \par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 )--India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday released data which showed that it heavily sold the greenback--a total of $2.9 billion--in November in a clear sign that it supported the rupee at the time when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumbled to a record low.\par \par \uc2 This largest monthly sale of the greenback in 32 months confirms the widely held view that the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  did protect the rupee in November, said Moses Harding, head of economic and market research at \uc2 IndusInd Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely remained heavy in December as well.\par \par \uc2 The rupee, Asia's worst-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2011, has borne the brunt of risk aversion stemming from the eurozone's sovereign debt crisis, which has magnified concerns about India's high inflation, slowing growth and the risk of an increase in the fiscal deficit.\par \par \uc2 The dollar surged to a record high of INR54.295 on Dec. 15. The local unit slumped about 7% against the greenback in November.\par \par \uc2 Subsequently, a slew of measures from Indian authorities to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation and increase dollar flows into local debt, apart from direct RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , helped the rupee recoup some of its losses.\par \par \uc2 The dollar, which was trading at INR51.69 at 1013 GMT Thursday, has lost nearly 3% against the local unit since the beginning of the year.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $943 million in October 2011 and $845 million in September, Reserve Bank data showed.\par \par \uc2 The RBI's dollar sales in November were the highest monthly sales since March 2009, when it sold a net $3.4 billion to protect the rupee amid the global financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 The RBI doesn't say whether it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and has a stated policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  only to manage exchange-rate volatility.\par \par \uc2 Last week, RBI Deputy Governor Subir Gokarn reiterated the stance that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't defend any particular rupee level, but added that it would "respond strongly to any sharp one-way moves" in the local unit.\par \par \uc2 The risk of depleting \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves has been cited by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an argument against defending the exchange rate through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Data released by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves shrank by $4.18 billion to $296.69 billion in the week ended Dec. 30, falling below $300 billion for the first time since February 2011 after reaching a record high of $320.80 billion in September 2011.\par \par \uc2 However, analysts say the current level of India's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves isn't a cause for concern as it far exceeds the current account deficit and short-term external liabilities. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   --By Sudeep Jain, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \uc2 \f2 ; 91 22 6145 6123; sudeep.jain@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 12, 2012 05:45 ET (10:45 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120112e81c002l6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
