\par\par \b \uc2 RBI's  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market Nov dlr sales highest in over 2.5 yrs\b0\par\par\uc2 372 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2012\par 10:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, Jan 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in November, for a third consecutive month, in its biggest sale of dollars in over two-and-half years, to arrest a sharp fall in the rupee.\par \par \uc2  The official figures, which are released with a lag, show the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's increasing discomfort with the local unit's sharp decline in recent months.\par \par \uc2  The RBI sold a net $2.92 billion in November, highest since March 2009, when dollar sales stood at $3.39 billion, according to data from the RBI's monthly statistical supplement released Thursday.\par \par \uc2   In November, it did not buy dollars, as was the case in the two previous months of October and September. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $943 million and $845 million respectively in those two months, the bulletin showed.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar sales in September had been its first after November 2010, RBI data showed.\par \par \uc2  During the month of November, the rupee suffered its worst monthly fall in 16 years, plunging nearly 7 percent as persistent dollar demand from importers and portfolio outflows on global risk aversion pounded the local unit. \par \par \uc2  The rupee had touched a then record-low of 52.73 to the dollar on Nov. 22, according to Thomson Reuters data and the unit's slide subsequently continued to reach a record-low of 54.30 on Dec. 15.\par \par \uc2 The rupee, which hit its 2011 peak of 43.85 in late July, began to subsequently fall as the local economy began to slow and the global economy hit a rough patch.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has maintained it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only to smoothen volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and without targeting a specific exchange rate on the rupee.\par \par \uc2     At 2:07 p.m. (0837 GMT) on Thursday, the partially convertible rupee was at 51.80/81 per dollar, 0.2 percent stronger than its Wednesday's close of 51.90/91.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government have taken steps to support the rupee in the past few months.\par \par \uc2  For a factbox, see  \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Aditya Phatak; Editing by Subhadip Sircar)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK-\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 /   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120112e81c000kw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
