\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  rupee ends up on inflows, likely RBI  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 576 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2012\par 03:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * RBI probably sold dollars around 51.74 level - traders\par \par \uc2 * Indian shares fall 0.9 percent, limiting rupee gains\par \par \uc2 * Current account gap seen weighing on rupee\par \par \uc2 * ECB meeting results awaited\par \par \uc2 By Shamik Paul\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Jan 12 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee closed higher on Thursday as foreign funds continued to invest in local debt, though weak domestic shares and dollar demand from oil importers put a lid on gains.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  probably sold dollars around the 51.74 rupee level in late trading, which further supported the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.\par \par \uc2 The rupee ended at 51.60/61 to the dollar, up from Wednesday's close of 51.90/91, rising as high as 51.52 after the suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The rupee's recent gains have been flow-driven, but the outlook is weak because the debt crisis in Europe is far from over," said S. Nagaraja, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing at Al Rostamani International Exchange.\par \par \uc2 "However, sharp volatility is unlikely because the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  will put a check on sharp moves in either direction," he added.\par \par \uc2 In an attempt to arrest the sharp slide of the rupee, the RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for a third consecutive month in November in its biggest sale of dollars in more two-and-half years, data released on Thursday showed.\par \par \uc2 Net inflows into Indian debt so far in January stand at about $2.07 billion, substantially more than the $387.15 million invested in equities, data from the Securities and Exchange Board of India showed.\par \par \uc2 Traders and economists expected the rupee to weaken in the weeks ahead on worries about India's current account deficit, and as investors remain wary of taking on risky assets.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of a country that runs a sustained trade deficit has to depreciate, \uc2 V. Balakrishnan\uc2 , chief financial of \uc2 Infosys Ltd\uc2 , said after India's No. 2 software exporter released quarterly results.\par \par \uc2 "India is seen as an emerging market risk," he said. "To that extent money is not coming in when the environment is very volatile," he said, adding India's political system is paralysed and no reforms are happening. "So if you put all this together, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to depreciate," Balakrishnan said.\par \par \uc2 (For a factbox on the steps taken by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government to stem the rupee's fall, see )\par \par \uc2 India's main share index closed down 0.9 percent after \uc2 Infosys\uc2  cut its full-year revenue forecast.\par \par \uc2 Strong factory data for November failed to allay concerns about economic growth.\par \par \uc2 Industrial production recovered in November, rising 5.9 percent from a year earlier. Traders are now awaiting December headline inflation data due on Monday for clues on what action, if any, the RBI will announce on Jan. 24\par \par \uc2 The euro edged up, helped by strong demand at an auction of Spanish bonds but it faces selling if the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is meeting on Thursday, hints at more interest rate cuts.\par \par \uc2 One-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts were quoted at 52.04, indicating some weakness in the short-term in the onshore spot rate.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most-traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and the United Stock Exchange were all around 51.8 on total volume of $4.3 billion.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Ted Kerr)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA/RUPEE (UPDATE 3)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120115e81c0001i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
