\par\par \uc2 Interview\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW: RBI To Respond To Sharp One-Way Moves In Indian Rupee\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gaurav Raghuvanshi,P.R. Venkat \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 564 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2012\par 10:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones Top News & Commentary\par \uc2 DJCOMM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 --RBI ready to smooth sharp rupee moves, deputy governor says\par \par \uc2 --Says rupee has stabilized, inflation and economic growth likely stable in 2012\par \par \uc2 --Rupee depreciation boosts inflation via higher fuel import bill, but fall in other commodities can cushion it\par \par \uc2 (Adds rupee fall in 4th paragraph, more comments from the official in 8th paragraph)\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 )--\b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stands ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to smooth any sharp move in the rupee, which is expected to stabilize after its recent fall, a Reserve Bank of India deputy governor said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "We will respond strongly to any sharp one-way moves" in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Subir Gokarn told \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 He said recent measures such as freeing for non-resident Indians and putting restrictions on forward hedging contracts have helped stabilize the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 The RBI acted after the rupee fell more than 15% against the U.s. dollar between September and mid-December and ended the year down 18.8% against the greenback, making it the worst performer among Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold some $4 billion-$5 billion in November to staunch the rupee's fall, according to calculations by \uc2 Kotak Mahindra Bank\uc2  . Gokarn said the RBI won't defend any particular rupee level and acts only to curb volatility.\par \par \uc2 The RBI aims to ensure that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements are not being distorted by speculation, but the precise rupee rate "is not something we have a view on," Gokarn said.\par \par \uc2 "Our whole approach to exchange-rate management has been driven by the need to ensure that our medium-term external situation is secure, while also not allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move uncontrollably," Gokarn said.\par \par \uc2 He said banking-system liquidity is tight but not at crisis levels, noting that money-market rates remain within the Liquidity Adjustment Facility corridor--the gap between the rates at which banks can park funds at the RBI and access money at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily liquidity facility.\par \par \uc2 India's economic growth slowed to its lowest level in more than two years in the July-September quarter at 6.9%, from 7.7% in April-June, hurt by high local borrowing costs and bhe deepening euro-zone crisis. Gokarn declined to give a prediction for Indian gross domestic product growth this year, saying the RBI will provide estimates in its monetary policy review later this month.\par \par \uc2 Gokarn said India's monetary cycle has peaked after 13 rate hikes from March 2010-October 2011 but that doesn't mean it will soon reverse, with prices remaining stubbornly high amid faltering global economic growth. The weaker rupee and high crude oil prices mean that risks to inflation haven't gone away, he said.\par \par \uc2 Earlier Thursday, speaking at an event organized by the \uc2 Institute of Southeast Asian Studies\uc2  in Singapore, Gokarn said the RBI "is very concerned" about the rupee's recent fall driving up the cost of India's fuel imports. But a decline in the prices of other commodities has had some mitigating impact, he said.\par \par \uc2 -By Gaurav Raghuvanshi; Dow Jones Newswires; +65 64154 154; gaurav.raghuvanshi@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 -Sudeep Jain in Mumbai contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 05, 2012 04:04 ET (09:04 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCOMM1120120105e815002ap\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
