\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee weak on local equities, importer demand\b0\par\par\uc2 225 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 2011\par 03:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, Dec 29 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee stayed weak on Thursday due to a sluggish local share market along with subdued global risk appetite ahead of an Italian debt auction, a key event which is expected to give cues on Europe's economic outlook.\par \par \uc2  * Dollar demand from oil importers for month-end payments and on account of defence payments kept the selling pressure on rupee, traders said.\par \par \uc2  * However, a big slide in the rupee was unlikely as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is  likely to step in and keep the local unit's fall under check by selling dollars, they said. The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  is suspected to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday helping rupee recover some losses.\par \par \uc2  * At 2:37 p.m. (0907 GMT), the rupee was at 53.33/34 to the dollar,\par \par \uc2 weaker than Wednesday's close of 53.07/08, and the unit is likely to stay in range of 53.25 to 53.50 in rest of the session.\par \par \uc2  * India's benchmark share index was down 0.4 percent while the euro fell to a fresh 10-year low against the yen on Thursday, driven by selling from Japanese retail investors and exporters.  \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Aditya Phatak; Editing by Subhadip Sircar)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA/RUPEE (UPDATE 2)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120101e7ct00016\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
