weakness in gold and spot iron-ore prices. \f28 \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton\f28 \uc2 \f2  lost 1.2% while \f28 \uc2 \f2 Newcrest Mining\f28 \uc2 \f2  dropped 2.5%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo Electric Power\f28 \uc2 \f2  lost 14.2% on comments by Japanese Trade and Industry Minister Yukio Edano late Tuesday that the utility needs to fundamentally rebuild its finances, and that it should consider all options, including temporary state control.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro continued to trade in tight ranges against the U.S. dollar and the Japanese yen amid holiday-thinned volumes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors were also cautiously eyeing an Italian bond auction later in the day as a gauge of whether distressed government bonds will be purchased by European banks after the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's cash infusion last week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was at $1.3071 against the greenback from $1.3068 late Tuesday in New York and at Y101.66 versus the yen from Y101.77. The dollar was at Y77.79 from Y77.89.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par METALS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spot gold was at $1,587.70 a troy ounce, down $4.60 from its previous settlement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par OIL SUMMARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 February Nymex crude oil futures were recently down 12 cents at $101.22 a barrel on Globex.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TOP HEADLINES \par US Consumer Confidence Jumps In December \par Obama To Name Two To Fill Fed Vacancies \par US Home Prices Decline In October \par Greece To Hold Elections At End Of April -Finance Minister \par Sears To Close Stores As Woes Continue \par Japan, China Leaders Focus On North Korea \par NYSE, Deutsche Boerse Extend Deal Deadline \par US Midwest Manufacturing Output Slips \par US Treasury Declines Once Again To Tag China As \f28 \b \highligh