\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee closes off lows as shares perk up\b0\par\par\uc2 501 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 2011\par 04:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Dollar demand from local oil companies weighs\par \par \uc2 * Volumes low due to year-end caution, recent RBI steps - traders\par \par \uc2 * Rupee seen at 53.10-53.15/dlr early next week - \uc2 Canara Bank\par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2 By Aditya Phatak\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Dec 22 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee closed weaker but off its intraday low on Thursday as domestic equities turned positive after early losses and on signs that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's massive loans to banks will avert a euro zone credit crunch for now.\par \par \uc2 Some traders cited dollar sales by foreign banks as a reason for the rupee's rebound, while others speculated about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Demand from oil importers limited the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The RBI is widely thought to have sold dollars on Dec. 15 after the rupee hit a record low of 54.30 to the dollar, and traders suspect it has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  intermittently ever since.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, RBI Governor Duvvuri Subbarao said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was monitoring \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets hourly and would step in to contain any sharp volatility.\par \par \uc2 "Who would want to invite the RBI's wrath, when room to manoeuvre in the market has already reduced drastically," said a trader at a private sector bank, referring to recent measures taken by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb speculative trading.\par \par \uc2 This, he said, was the main reason that players cut their long dollar positions once the euro and equities reversed course.\par \par \uc2 "Everybody is afraid of that phone call (from the RBI)," he said.\par \par \uc2 (For details on steps taken by the RBI to curb the rupee's volatility and increase inflows see: )\par \par \uc2 The euro is seen as the main gauge of global risk sentiment, so is closely tracked by traders in emerging markets such as India.\par \par \uc2 The rupee ended at 52.72/73 to the dollar, down from Wednesday's close of 52.49/50. It hit a low of 52.90.\par \par \uc2 Demand from oil importers, the largest buyers of dollars in the domestic market, kept the rupee under pressure for most of the session.\par \par \uc2 "Risk sentiment is still jittery and dollar demand from oil companies has been persistent," said Ravi Kumar, manager foreign dealer at \uc2 Canara Bank\uc2 . "Rupee could weaken to around 53.10-53.15 next week as month-end demand from oil companies rises."\par \par \uc2 Traders said volumes in the dollar-rupee market have fallen sharply due to a combination of the RBI's curbs on trading limits on Dec. 15 and caution ahead of book closures on Dec. 31.\par \par \uc2 One-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts were quoted at 53.19, indicating more short-term weakness in the onshore spot rate.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most-traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and the United Stock Exchange closed around 52.77, with total volume at $3.76 billion.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA/(UPDATE 3)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111225e7cm0001g\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intb